{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"All six unit-test runners and all eight RVFI trace comparisons pass. CoreMark passes CRC, bounded-access, and marker checks at 4,491,485 measured cycles; the measured fitness is 160.80, above 159.63006.\n\nThe deep DIV trace shows a reference-model signedness mismatch: for `0xc2000000 / 0x62800000`, the core returns the correct signed quotient 0, while the model expects unsigned quotient 1. Yosys marks the model’s divide operands unsigned. I’m documenting this failure and retaining the unchanged formal contract.\n"}}
