{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*test*' cores/bench/test; cat cores/bench/core.yaml; cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 41.241\n  lut4: 2806\n  ff: 663\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\n  updated: '2026-10-02T06:05:01.728489Z'\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r1s1 (improvement, +657.59%): Moving combinational ALU `/` and `%` into a shared four-bit-per-cycle, eight-cycle divider removes full-division depth from the EX timing path, letting clock-rate gains outweigh CoreMark's added divide stalls.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.25%): A 64-entry BHT plus early JAL cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.45% at nearly unchanged Fmax (5.514 MHz), but lost to iterative division because prediction left the combinational DIV/REM timing bottleneck intact.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'for p in /AGENTS.md /srv/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/AGENTS.md; do if test -f \"$p\"; then cat \"$p\"; fi; done; cat test/_helpers.py; cat cores/bench/test/conftest.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'for p in /AGENTS.md /srv/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/AGENTS.md; do if test -f \"$p\"; then cat \"$p\"; fi; done; cat test/_helpers.py; cat cores/bench/test/conftest.py'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Shared cocotb constants and runner helpers for unit tests.\n\nConstants mirror rtl/core_pkg.sv. If a localparam there changes, change\nthe matching value here.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# cocotb 2.x moved the runner from cocotb.runner to cocotb_tools.runner.\nfrom cocotb_tools.runner import get_runner\n\n# ── ALU encodings (rtl/core_pkg.sv) ────────────────────────────────────────\nALU_ADD    = 0\nALU_SUB    = 1\nALU_AND    = 2\nALU_OR     = 3\nALU_XOR    = 4\nALU_SLT    = 5\nALU_SLTU   = 6\nALU_SLL    = 7\nALU_SRL    = 8\nALU_SRA    = 9\nALU_LUI    = 10\n# RV32M ops use op[4]=1 and op[2:0]=funct3 (matches core_pkg.sv):\nALU_MUL    = 0b10000  # 16\nALU_MULH   = 0b10001  # 17\nALU_MULHSU = 0b10010  # 18\nALU_MULHU  = 0b10011  # 19\nALU_DIV    = 0b10100  # 20\nALU_DIVU   = 0b10101  # 21\nALU_REM    = 0b10110  # 22\nALU_REMU   = 0b10111  # 23\n\n# ── BranchOp encodings (= funct3 of BRANCH opcode) ─────────────────────────\nBR_BEQ  = 0\nBR_BNE  = 1\nBR_BLT  = 4\nBR_BGE  = 5\nBR_BLTU = 6\nBR_BGEU = 7\n\n# ── Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nRTL       = REPO_ROOT / \"rtl\"\nTEST_DIR  = REPO_ROOT / \"test\"\nSIM_BUILD = REPO_ROOT / \"sim_build\"\n\n\ndef run_cocotb(toplevel: str, sources: list[str], test_module: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Build the DUT under Verilator and run the given cocotb test_module.\n\n    `sources` is a list of bare filenames under rtl/. Order matters —\n    package files (e.g. core_pkg.sv) come first.\n    \"\"\"\n    sim = os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\")\n    runner = get_runner(sim)\n    build_dir = SIM_BUILD / toplevel\n\n    runner.build(\n        sources=[str(RTL / s) for s in sources],\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n        always=True,\n        build_args=[\"-Wall\", \"-Wno-fatal\", \"-Wno-style\"],\n    )\n    runner.test(\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        test_module=test_module,\n        test_dir=str(TEST_DIR),\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n    )\n\"\"\"pytest configuration for cocotb unit tests.\n\nAdds this directory to sys.path so test_*.py modules can `import _helpers`\nduring pytest collection. Cocotb sets PYTHONPATH separately for the\nsimulator-side import.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n_HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nif str(_HERE) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HERE))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
