CORE_NAME-$$\", but an\n# agent's sandboxed shell runs in its own PID namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n# for every agent, so siblings wrote into one dir and wiped each other's\n# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n# FORMAL_WORK_ID pins the suffix so tools/eval/formal.py can remove exactly\n# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core\n…[62215 of 65287 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9e1763b58732a8f6]…\ness\": 91.19, \"delta_pct\": -0.69, \"vs_baseline\": 652.39, \"fmax_mhz\": 38.315, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201709, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3211, \"ff\": 792, \"seeds\": [38.305, 38.315, 38.315], \"perturbations\": [[0, 38.305, 35], [1, 38.315, 33], [2, 38.315, 33]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s1\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -21.106, \"arrival_ns\": 31.401, \"logic_cells\": 138, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 35, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T06:27:07.792518Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r2s2 (regression, -0.69%): The 64-entry BHT plus early JAL reduced CoreMark cycles by 6.45%, but a 7.1% Fmax loss (41.241 to 38.315 MHz) outweighed the savings with the worst path still through divider quotient_q and EX, so predictor integration must preserve timing outside the fetch path.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
