ill lost to validity-only squashing at 52.313 MHz.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-001-r4s0 (regression, -3.79%): Balanced masked-OR ALU/EX selection with `syn_keep` cut post-multiply LUT depth from seven to five, but routing left selection delay near 6 ns and median Fmax fell from 52.313 to 50.326 MHz with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r4s1 (improvement, +8.78%): Capturing fully forwarded operands in ID/EX and forcing flop register-file storage with `syn_ramstyle = \"registers\"` removes late forwarding from EX arithmetic paths, improving timing without extra CoreMark cycles at increased LUT/flip-flop cost.\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu_altops.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\ncores/bench/core.yaml\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\ncores/bench/experiments/.gitkeep\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
