{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python -u - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all,summarize\nfrom pathlib import Path\nbase=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dbbcb5d7')\ndef run(name):\n p=base/name\n r=build_all(Path.cwd(),p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',p/'timing')\n (p/'timing_result.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\n print(name,json.dumps(summarize(r)),flush=True)\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3) as pool:\n list(pool.map(run,('r10_payloadreset','r10_signedpredecode','r10_linkpredecode')))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"r10_payloadreset {\"placement_failed\": false, \"fmax_mhz\": 60.963, \"seeds\": [59.825, 60.963, 60.963], \"perturbations\": [[0, 59.825, 14], [1, 60.963, 18], [2, 60.963, 18]], \"lut4\": 5136, \"ff\": 2253, \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_uu_63_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -11.715, \"arrival_ns\": 21.789, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}}\nr10_linkpredecode {\"placement_failed\": false, \"fmax_mhz\": 71.864, \"seeds\": [74.977, 71.864, 71.864], \"perturbations\": [[0, 74.977, 11], [1, 71.864, 17], [2, 71.864, 17]], \"lut4\": 5085, \"ff\": 2210, \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.is_auipc_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_ss_63_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -8.337, \"arrival_ns\": 18.411, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}}\nr10_signedpredecode {\"placement_failed\": false, \"fmax_mhz\": 71.608, \"seeds\": [69.798, 71.608, 71.608], \"perturbations\": [[0, 69.798, 10], [1, 71.608, 10], [2, 71.608, 10]], \"lut4\": 5186, \"ff\": 2210, \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_if/count_q_2_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/queue_q[0]_63_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.327, \"arrival_ns\": 19.621, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_69", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r10s0',\n 'title':'Precompute jump write eligibility before ID/EX capture',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion's critical paths include EX arithmetic/control through operand forwarding back into ID. The current trap-adjusted producer enable can depend on branch outcome and jump target alignment, despite conditional branches never writing a register. Prior r8s2 changed the combinational producer predicate and regressed. Instead, move the small jump-alignment calculation to the existing ID capture boundary and register the complete write-eligibility bit with its operands. This targets the late control path without changing prediction or pipeline cadence.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Add one write_eligible bit to id_ex_t. Compute it in ID from the validated decoder controls, the fully forwarded rs1_resolved value, the selected instruction's PC, and its decoded immediate. Let jump_low be the two-bit modular sum (dec_is_jalr ? rs1_resolved[1:0] : in.pc[1:0]) + imm[1:0]. A JALR link is eligible when jump_low[1] is zero because architectural JALR clears bit zero. A direct JAL link requires jump_low == 0. Capture write_eligible = dec_reg_write && (\"'!dec_is_jump || link_aligned) under exactly the existing ID/EX payload enable. Reset it with the existing ID/EX bundle; retain it with the operands during backend/load-use holds. Conditional branches and illegal instructions remain non-producers through the unmodified validated decoder.\n\nChange only the EX forwarding enable to in.valid && in.write_eligible && !in.ctrl.mem_read && (!is_divide || div_result_valid). Preserve every existing architectural trap computation, ctrl_with_trap field, EX/MEM write control, branch resolution, redirect, predictor training, result-data mux and divider request/completion equation. The registered eligibility bit is a timing replica for operand forwarding, not a replacement for architectural exception detection. In particular, misaligned JAL/JALR must neither forward nor write a link. The existing load-use interlock guarantees resolved operands are complete before ID capture; validity-only recovery still annuls wrong-path entries. No register-file, arithmetic, fetch-queue, predictor-policy, pipeline-depth or retirement-width changes belong in this hypothesis.\n\nThis is one local control-precomputation micro-optimization. It moves a two-bit alignment check before an existing register and removes full branch/jump fault resolution from the subsequent forwarding-enable path. It adds one payload flip-flop, no instruction cycle and no new state machine. Decoder reg_write is false for every conditional branch; retain and check that property rather than weakening the trap rules. The low-bit sum must include the carry from bit zero, including odd JALR operands and immediates. Do not substitute only rs1[1] XOR imm[1].\n\nA temporary implementation passed all 33 existing pipeline cocotb tests. Full timing and CoreMark validation are pending; the predicted gain is not measured. Prior local bypass, shared-multiplier, register-file and operand-mux probes in this session lowered Fmax and are excluded. The new ID-side forwarding-to-alignment path, divider launch and placement may erase this candidate'\"'s gain. Preserve nret=1, all core ports and every hard invariant.\n\nProve eligibility equivalent to the existing producer predicate for all reachable decoder outputs and every low-bit operand/PC/immediate combination. Test aligned/misaligned JAL and JALR, all odd JALR low-bit combinations, branch encoding source aliases, EX/MEM/WB-dependent JALR operands, dependent link consumers, x0, load-use and divide completion, backend holds, redirects and reset. Run the unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation. Expect exactly 3978988 bracketed cycles; acceptance requires fitness above 200.06842 iterations/s and median Gowin Fmax above 79.607 MHz at that cycle count. Normal formal and timing measurements remain required before acceptance.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n  {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add a one-bit write_eligible payload field to id_ex_t only; keep the top-level contract and other pipeline bundles unchanged.'},\n  {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute exact two-bit JAL/JALR target alignment from fully forwarded operands and capture decoded write eligibility under the existing payload/reset/hold protocol.'},\n  {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use the captured eligibility bit for fwd_w_en, retaining valid, load exclusion and completed-divide gating. Keep all architectural trap and EX/MEM write-control equations unchanged.'},\n  {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add directed forwarded-JALR and link-consumer tests spanning all low-bit operand/immediate pairs, alignment traps, x0, competing producers and holds. Retain all existing predictor, queue, arithmetic, memory and RVFI assertions.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated schema-valid hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
