{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor ln in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n e=json.loads(ln)\n print(e['id'], e.get('category'),e.get('title'),e.get('outcome'),e.get('fmax_mhz'),e.get('cycles'))\n if e.get('category')=='micro_opt' and e['id'] \"'!='\"'baseline-bench-bccc675':\n  h=e.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',e.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-bccc675 micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench improvement 5.442 4491485\nhyp-20261002-001-r1s0 micro_opt Share DIV and REM through a fused-subtract unsigned divider regression 3.887 4491485\nPROPOSAL: Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one combinational\nunsigned restoring divider that produces both quotient and remainder.\nFor DIV and REM, convert operands to unsigned two's-complement magnitudes;\nfor DIVU and REMU, use the original unsigned operands. Restore the quotient\nsign from a[31] XOR b[31], and the remainder sign from a[31], only for the\nsigned operations. Select quotient versus remainder after the shared core.\n\nImplement the divider as 32 statically unrolled, progressively sized stages.\nStarting with R_0 = 0, stage k = 1..32 forms the k-bit trial remainder\nT_k = {R_(k-1), magnitude_a[32-k]}. Compute a single (k+1)-bit unsigned\ndifference D_k = {1'b0, T_k} - {1'b0, magnitude_b[k-1:0]}. Accept it only\nwhen all divisor bits above k-1 are zero and D_k[k] is zero. The accepted\ndecision is quotient[32-k]; R_k is D_k[k-1:0] if accepted, otherwise T_k.\nAt k=32 the upper-divisor-zero condition is constant true. Use static\ngenerate widths, with an explicit first stage, and share the upper-bit\nnonzero reductions. Derive the comparison directly from the subtraction's\nborrow bit; do not infer a separat