pu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r11s0',\n 'title':'Use parallel prefix-OR conditional negation for divider magnitudes',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 191.27 iterations/s at 76.107 MHz with 3978988 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent micro_opt operation-decode changes regressed and timing repeatedly exposed signed magnitude preparation followed by the launch prefix. Prior carry-select work changed ordinary ADD/SUB, and the r8 prefix lookup changed the prefix itself; neither replaced the conditional magnitude negation. Target this local normalization circuit while preserving the divider schedule and prefix.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace only the real divider's two conditional signed-magnitude expressions with an exact parallel prefix-OR conditional-negation network. For an input x and negate flag n=signed_op && x[31], compute magnitude[0]=x[0]. For i=1..31, compute lower_nonzero[i]=OR(x[i-1:0]) and magnitude[i]=x[i] XOR (n AND lower_nonzero[i]). Generate this network independently for m_a and m_b using explicit constant-width slices. Signed mode remains the existing exact ALU_DIV/ALU_REM decode. When n=0 the result is x; when n=1 this implements two's-complement -x modulo 2\"'^32 by preserving every bit through the least-significant one and complementing all more significant bits. In particular zero stays zero and INT_MIN has unsigned magnitude 0x80000000.\n\nThe lower-nonzero reductions depend only on raw registered M operands, not on signed_op. Arrange their shared reductions as balanced prefix-OR logic rather than a serial 31-stage recurrence. The signed-mode signal enters the final AND/XOR bit function; do not express this again as a full subtractor followed by a magnitude mux. Use portable synthesizable RTL, with no timing constraints, vendor primitives, keep attributes or undefined values. This is one local combinational arithmetic implementation change, with no extra state or pipeline stage.\n\nFeed these exact magnitudes to the unchanged launch-prefix arithmetic, small-divisor guard and widened divisor-multiple bank. Preserve the first four quotient bits computed at acceptance, seven subsequent full-width radix-16 busy iterations, registered completion, earliest t8 handshake, sticky backpressure, reset cancellation, captured signs, original dividend and zero-divisor override. Leave result sign correction unchanged. Preserve all multiply and integer operators, direct M inputs, ALTOPS formulas and timing, EX forwarding and holds, predictor/FIFO behavior, decoder legality, nret=1, memory handshakes and all RVFI contracts. No execution-latency or retirement change is part of the proposal.\n\nThe intended benefit is replacing the carry-propagating negate plus conditional selection ahead of the prefix and divisor multiples with raw-input prefix reductions and a shallow final conditional XOR. This differs from the unsuccessful ordinary carry-select adders and operation-decode retiming. Extra prefix fanout and routing may negate the benefit, and ordinary ALU feedback remains a competing limit. Predict six percent higher fitness with low confidence pending vendor measurement. The acceptance threshold is strictly above 200.06842 iterations/s, approximately 79.607 MHz median Fmax if cycles remain unchanged. Source-level logic depth alone does not establish a gain.\n\nRetain all existing real-arithmetic, ALTOPS and pipeline checks. Add exact signed/unsigned magnitude and final DIV/REM vectors with the least-significant set bit at every position, powers of two and neighbors, zero, INT_MIN, UINT_MAX, alternating patterns and deterministic random values. Compare magnitudes against Python integer negation masked to 32 bits, and check the existing post-launch quotient/remainder state and final arithmetic results. Keep live-input isolation, seven-iteration/t8 timing, backpressure, reset, dependency and progress assertions unchanged. Run the unchanged formal and full RVFI cosimulation gates and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation with both stall streams. Expect exactly 3978988 timed cycles. ALTOPS formal does not prove this real normalization network; real arithmetic coverage remains mandatory and formal-deep remains available.\n\nExploratory alternatives in this proposal session were measured separately and are excluded: AUIPC sum routing, local predictor-counter updates, redundant x0-mask removal, preselected operand registers, a shared shifter, and first-byte divider iteration rebalancing all regressed median Fmax. The final proposal changes only conditional magnitude generation.'\"''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Replace only dividend_magnitude and divisor_magnitude conditional negations with the exact raw-operand prefix-OR/conditional-XOR identity. Preserve the entire prefix, multiple bank, recurrence, completion controller, result correction, all other operations and ALTOPS branch.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain every existing arithmetic and protocol assertion. Add independent magnitude/reference and final DIV/REM checks spanning each least-significant-one position, sign/zero/overflow boundaries and random operands, while retaining exact launch state and t8 completion checks.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Replaced and validated',p)\nPY\nRTL_DIR=/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/magnitude_probe/rtl OBJ_DIR=/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/magnitude_probe/obj_dir NRET=1 bash test/cosim/build.sh > /srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/magnitude_probe/cosim_build.log 2>&1\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
