quotient/remainder state and final arithmetic results. Keep live-input isolation, seven-iteration/t8 timing, backpressure, reset, dependency and progress assertions unchanged. Run the unchanged formal and full RVFI cosimulation gates and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation with both stall streams. Expect exactly 3978988 timed cycles. ALTOPS formal does not prove this real normalization network; real arithmetic coverage remains mandatory and formal-deep remains available.\n\nExploratory alternatives in this proposal session were measured separately and are excluded: AUIPC sum routing, local predictor-counter updates, redundant x0-mask removal, preselected operand registers, a shared shifter, and first-byte divider iteration rebalancing all regressed median Fmax. The final proposal changes only conditional magnitude generation.'\"''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Replace only dividend_magnitude and divisor_magnitude conditional negations with the exact raw-operand prefix-OR/conditional-XOR identity. Preserve the entire prefix, multiple bank, recurrence, completion controller, result correction, all other operations and ALTOPS branch.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain every existing arithmetic and protocol assertion. Add independent magnitude/reference and final DIV/REM checks spanning each least-significant-one position, sign/zero/overflow boundaries and random operands, while retaining exact launch state and t8 completion checks.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Replaced and validated',p)\nPY\nRTL_DIR=/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/magnitude_probe/rtl OBJ_DIR=/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/magnitude_probe/obj_dir NRET=1 bash test/cosim/build.sh > /srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/magnitude_probe/cosim_build.log 2>&1\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"The full-width prefix network passed the existing tests but regressed timing. I’m narrowing it to the dividend’s leading nibble: compute just those four magnitude bits from lower-bit OR reductions, leaving divisor normalization and the lower dividend bits unchanged. This reduces the added logic while targeting the carry path into the launch prefix."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/nibble_probe')\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl',root/'rtl',dirs_exist_ok=True)\np=root/'rtl/alu.sv'\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('  logic [31:0] dividend_magnitude, divisor_magnitude;','  logic [31:0] dividend_magnitude, divisor_magnitude;\\\\n  logic [3:0] dividend_prefix;\\\\n  logic dividend_lower_nonzero;\\\\n  assign dividend_lower_nonzero = |m_a[27:0];\\\\n  assign dividend_prefix[0] = m_a[28] \"'^ (signed_op && m_a[31] && dividend_lower_nonzero);'\"\\\\n  for (genvar k = 1; k < 4; k++) begin : prefix_magnitude_bit\\\\n    assign dividend_prefix[k] = m_a[28+k] \"'^ (signed_op && m_a[31] && (dividend_lower_nonzero || (|m_a[27+k:28])));'\"\\\\n  end')\ns=s.replace('dividend_magnitude[31:28]','dividend_prefix')\np.write_text(s)\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/test',root/'test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nPY\npython -u - <<'PY'\nfrom tools.eval import gowin\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/dd8a7533/nibble_probe')\nresults=gowin.build_all(Path.cwd(),root/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',root/'timing')\n(root/'timing.json').write_text(json.dumps(results,indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(gowin.summarize(results),indent=2), flush=True)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
