{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Flatten EX result selection and remove redundant divide gating from scalar data',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 224.83 iterations/s at 89.575 MHz. Ordinary EX-to-ID arithmetic feedback competes with branch recovery and divider recurrence. Its integer result currently passes through nested divide-versus-link-versus-ALU selection before ID forwarding. The scalar ALU already returns zero for all DIV/REM opcodes, so the divide classification need not gate that scalar data path. Recent micro_opt r13s0 failed to improve this parent with divider threshold muxes; r9s0 carry select and r10s0 registered ALU decode also regressed. Target only the final EX result merge, without changing arithmetic or adding decode registers.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the nested conditional expression driving ex_stage.fwd_data with a parallel masked-OR merge of three existing results. Define select_div=is_divide, select_link=\"'!is_divide && in.ctrl.is_jump and select_scalar=!in.ctrl.is_jump. Then drive:\n  fwd_data = ({32{select_div}} & div_result)\n           | ({32{select_link}} & (in.pc + 32'\"'d4))\n           | ({32{select_scalar}} & alu_result).\nKeep select signals combinational, without keep/preserve attributes or extra registers. All values are full-width 32-bit quantities.\n\nThe scalar mask deliberately omits \"'!is_divide. This is an exact data-dependent simplification, not an assumption that overlapping selects are harmless. is_divide implies one of the four DIV/REM ALU opcodes, and alu.sv'\"'s ordinary out is exactly zero for every such opcode in both real and ALTOPS builds. Thus a selected divide ORs its result with zero. For non-divides, the link/scalar masks partition the result exactly as the original mux. Keeping \"'!is_divide in select_link preserves divide priority even for inconsistent internal control bundles. The rewrite is equivalent to the old expression for all input states satisfying the existing is_divide definition and scalar ALU function, without needing branch-versus-jump decoder exclusivity.\n\nApply the result to the same two consumers: EX-to-ID forwarding and EX/MEM.alu_result. Keep fwd_w_en and all producer eligibility unchanged. Do not add valid/reset/ready/redirect qualification to these data masks, change source tags, or alter youngest-producer priority. Invalid payload data remains inert under existing valid controls. Preserve the ALU case statement, scalar operand muxes, PC+4 adder, AUIPC, multiplier, full radix-32 divider, t8 request/result schedule and all real/ALTOPS formulas. Retain branch comparison, alignment traps, recovery/training, memory-request preparation, queue, all holds, nret=1 ports, legality, exact-once retirement and every contract invariant.\n\nThis is a local combinational result-selection micro-optimization. It removes divide classification from the scalar mask and gives Gowin an explicit parallel merge instead of serial priority selection. The older r4s0 broad ALU/EX masked-OR experiment regressed with an unregistered multiplier and syn_keep constraints; this proposal changes only the present post-arithmetic EX merge and uses no preservation attributes. The risk remains that Gowin already optimizes the priority mux, or that routing and other near-critical paths erase the gain.\n\nAn exploratory fully masked merge, which still included !is_divide in the scalar mask, reached 90.388 MHz in placement option 1, versus 89.575 MHz champion median. That small preliminary change does not demonstrate acceptance. The final proposal additionally removes the redundant divide gate; its full three-placement timing is pending. No gain is claimed as measured until that result and unchanged canonical CoreMark validation complete. Expect 3984075 marker-delimited cycles; acceptance requires strictly above 235.17218 iterations/s, about 93.695 MHz at unchanged cycles.\n\nRetain all existing tests and validate ordinary integer operations, AUIPC/LUI, jumps and link dependencies, real/ALTOPS division completion, immediate consumers, x0, producer priority, reset and both memory stalls. Specifically establish that scalar out is zero for all DIV/REM opcodes while the registered divide result is nonzero, including operand and opcode changes after request acceptance. Test sticky completion, trap-suppressed jump links and wrong-path effects. Require unchanged normal formal, full small-program RVFI cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and all three Gowin placement options. Arithmetic algorithms and timing are unchanged; retain the real-arithmetic checks and formal-deep obligation.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace only fwd_data priority selection with the specified three masked terms. Omit divide gating from the scalar mask because ordinary ALU out is zero for DIV/REM. Preserve divide priority in the link mask, all data widths, eligibility, registers, instruction timing and every other EX equation.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing architectural, forwarding, stall and latency assertions. Add focused selection coverage for scalar results, jump links and nonzero completed divides, including immediate consumers, trap-suppressed links, x0, held completion, reset and invalid/wrong-path instructions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain every real arithmetic and protocol assertion. Explicitly check ordinary out==0 for each DIV/REM opcode independently of the completed div_result, including nonzero quotient/remainder results, to guard the scalar-mask simplification.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu_altops.py','description':'Retain every ALTOPS formula and handshake check. Verify ordinary out remains zero for all divide/remainder opcodes while the nonzero registered ALTOPS result is available.'}\n]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef repr_str(dumper,data):return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,repr_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Overwrote and validated final single-angle proposal')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r14s0',\n'title':'Flatten EX result selection and remove redundant divide gating from scalar data',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 224.83 iterations/s at 89.575 MHz. Ordinary EX-to-ID arithmetic feedback competes with branch recovery and divider recurrence. Its integer result currently passes through nested divide-versus-link-versus-ALU selection before ID forwarding. The scalar ALU already returns zero for all DIV/REM opcodes, so the divide classification need not gate that scalar data path. Recent micro_opt r13s0 failed to improve this parent with divider threshold muxes; r9s0 carry select and r10s0 registered ALU decode also regressed. Target only the final EX result merge, without changing arithmetic or adding decode registers.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the nested conditional expression driving ex_stage.fwd_data with a parallel masked-OR merge of three existing results. Define select_div=is_divide, select_link=\"'!is_divide && in.ctrl.is_jump and select_scalar=!in.ctrl.is_jump. Then drive:\n  fwd_data = ({32{select_div}} & div_result)\n           | ({32{select_link}} & (in.pc + 32'\"'d4))\n           | ({32{select_scalar}} & alu_result).\nKeep select signals combinational, without keep/preserve attributes or extra registers. All values are full-width 32-bit quantities.\n\nThe scalar mask deliberately omits \"'!is_divide. This is an exact data-dependent simplification, not an assumption that overlapping selects are harmless. is_divide implies one of the four DIV/REM ALU opcodes, and alu.sv'\"'s ordinary out is exactly zero for every such opcode in both real and ALTOPS builds. Thus a selected divide ORs its result with zero. For non-divides, the link/scalar masks partition the result exactly as the original mux. Keeping \"'!is_divide in select_link preserves divide priority even for inconsistent internal control bundles. The rewrite is equivalent to the old expression for all input states satisfying the existing is_divide definition and scalar ALU function, without needing branch-versus-jump decoder exclusivity.\n\nApply the result to the same two consumers: EX-to-ID forwarding and EX/MEM.alu_result. Keep fwd_w_en and all producer eligibility unchanged. Do not add valid/reset/ready/redirect qualification to these data masks, change source tags, or alter youngest-producer priority. Invalid payload data remains inert under existing valid controls. Preserve the ALU case statement, scalar operand muxes, PC+4 adder, AUIPC, multiplier, full radix-32 divider, t8 request/result schedule and all real/ALTOPS formulas. Retain branch comparison, alignment traps, recovery/training, memory-request preparation, queue, all holds, nret=1 ports, legality, exact-once retirement and every contract invariant.\n\nThis is a local combinational result-selection micro-optimization. It removes divide classification from the scalar mask and gives Gowin an explicit parallel merge instead of serial priority selection. The older r4s0 broad ALU/EX masked-OR experiment regressed with an unregistered multiplier and syn_keep constraints; this proposal changes only the present post-arithmetic EX merge and uses no preservation attributes. The risk remains that Gowin already optimizes the priority mux, or that routing and other near-critical paths erase the gain.\n\nAn exploratory fully masked merge, which still included !is_divide in the scalar mask, reached 90.388 MHz in placement option 1, versus 89.575 MHz champion median. That small preliminary change does not demonstrate acceptance. The final proposal additionally removes the redundant divide gate; its full three-placement timing is pending. No gain is claimed as measured until that result and unchanged canonical CoreMark validation complete. Expect 3984075 marker-delimited cycles; acceptance requires strictly above 235.17218 iterations/s, about 93.695 MHz at unchanged cycles.\n\nRetain all existing tests and validate ordinary integer operations, AUIPC/LUI, jumps and link dependencies, real/ALTOPS division completion, immediate consumers, x0, producer priority, reset and both memory stalls. Specifically establish that scalar out is zero for all DIV/REM opcodes while the registered divide result is nonzero, including operand and opcode changes after request acceptance. Test sticky completion, trap-suppressed jump links and wrong-path effects. Require unchanged normal formal, full small-program RVFI cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and all three Gowin placement options. Arithmetic algorithms and timing are unchanged; retain the real-arithmetic checks and formal-deep obligation.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace only fwd_data priority selection with the specified three masked terms. Omit divide gating from the scalar mask because ordinary ALU out is zero for DIV/REM. Preserve divide priority in the link mask, all data widths, eligibility, registers, instruction timing and every other EX equation.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing architectural, forwarding, stall and latency assertions. Add focused selection coverage for scalar results, jump links and nonzero completed divides, including immediate consumers, trap-suppressed links, x0, held completion, reset and invalid/wrong-path instructions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain every real arithmetic and protocol assertion. Explicitly check ordinary out==0 for each DIV/REM opcode independently of the completed div_result, including nonzero quotient/remainder results, to guard the scalar-mask simplification.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu_altops.py','description':'Retain every ALTOPS formula and handshake check. Verify ordinary out remains zero for all divide/remainder opcodes while the nonzero registered ALTOPS result is available.'}\n]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef repr_str(dumper,data):return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,repr_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Overwrote and validated final single-angle proposal')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Overwrote and validated final single-angle proposal\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
