{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"The strongest probe so far is a parallel EX result merge at 90.388 MHz in placement option 1. Removing an additional gate made it slower. I’ll retain the fully masked version and report the evidence candidly: its gain is small, and it has not demonstrated the required 4.6% margin."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Flatten the final EX result mux into three disjoint masked paths'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 224.83 iterations/s at 89.575 MHz. Ordinary EX-to-ID arithmetic feedback competes with branch recovery and divider recurrence. Its existing scalar result passes through nested divide-versus-link-versus-ALU selection before ID forwarding. Recent micro_opt r13s0 failed to improve this parent with divider threshold muxes; r9s0 carry select and r10s0 registered ALU decode also regressed. Target only the final EX result merge, leaving arithmetic operators and decode registers unchanged.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace only the nested conditional expression driving ex_stage.fwd_data with a parallel masked-OR merge of three existing results. Define select_div=is_divide, select_link=\"'!is_divide && in.ctrl.is_jump and select_scalar=!is_divide && !in.ctrl.is_jump. Then drive:\n  fwd_data = ({32{select_div}} & div_result)\n           | ({32{select_link}} & (in.pc + 32'\"'d4))\n           | ({32{select_scalar}} & alu_result).\nUse exactly these pairwise-disjoint, exhaustive masks. Retain all three qualifications, even when architectural invariants could prove some redundant. Keep the signals combinational, without keep/preserve attributes or extra registers. All values are full-width 32-bit quantities. The expression must be bit-for-bit equivalent to the existing priority selection for arbitrary controls and data, including invalid payloads.\n\nApply the result to its same two consumers: EX-to-ID forwarding and EX/MEM.alu_result. Keep fwd_w_en and all producer eligibility unchanged. Do not add valid/reset/ready/redirect qualification to the masks, change source tags, or alter youngest-producer priority. Invalid payloads remain inert under existing validity controls. Preserve the ALU case statement, scalar operand muxes, PC+4 adder, AUIPC, multiplier, complete radix-32 divider, earliest t8 acceptance and both real/ALTOPS formulas. Retain branch comparison, alignment traps, recovery/training, prepared memory requests, queue, all holds, nret=1 ports, decoder legality, exact-once retirement and every contract invariant.\n\nThis is one local combinational result-selection micro-optimization. Explicit parallel selection may let Gowin combine masking with adjacent LUT logic and reduce serial selection/routing between arithmetic and operand capture. The older r4s0 broad ALU/EX masked-OR experiment regressed with an unregistered multiplier and syn_keep constraints; this proposal changes only the present final EX merge and uses no preservation attributes. Synthesis may already optimize the priority mux, and routing or other near-critical paths may erase the gain.\n\nA temporary implementation of this exact expression reached 90.388 MHz in Gowin placement option 1, using 6588 LUTs and 2801 registers, zero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. This is only about 0.91 percent above the recorded champion median, and does NOT demonstrate the required 4.6 percent acceptance margin. All three placements and canonical CoreMark validation are being checked. Predict one percent improvement with low confidence; do not describe the proposal as an accepted gain. Expected marker-delimited cycles are 3984075. Acceptance requires strictly more than 235.17218 iterations/s, approximately 93.695 MHz at unchanged cycles.\n\nA variant removing \"'!is_divide from the scalar mask reached only 86.327 MHz median and is excluded. Other isolated branch-qualification, AUIPC-routing, forwarding-selection, scalar sharing, smaller-divider and bank-reset probes also failed to beat the champion. None belongs in this proposal; do not bundle their changes with the final EX merge.\n\nRetain every existing arithmetic, architectural, forwarding, stall and latency assertion. Verify the mask expression against the original mux across all control combinations and arbitrary data. Exercise ordinary integer operations, AUIPC/LUI, jump links and dependencies, nonzero divide results and immediate consumers, x0, producer priority, trap-suppressed links, wrong-path effects, reset and both memory stalls. Require unchanged normal formal, full small-program RVFI cosimulation, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and all three Gowin placements. Full formal has not been run during hypothesis generation and remains required; no arithmetic algorithm or execution schedule changes.'\"'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':1,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace only fwd_data priority selection with the specified three mutually exclusive full-width masked terms and their OR. Keep both \"'!is_divide qualifications, existing operands, eligibility, registers, timing and every other EX equation.'\"'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing architectural, forwarding, stall and latency assertions. Add focused result-selection checks for scalar operations, jump links and nonzero completed divides, including immediate consumers, x0, held completion, reset, trap-suppressed links and wrong-path effects. Verify disjoint mask behavior against the original priority mux.'}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dumper,s:dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90));jsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Final hypothesis saved and schema-valid')\nPY\npytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
