{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261002-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Move decode stall to the final fetch-queue payload selection\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion reaches 224.83 iterations/s at 89.575 MHz. Prior micro_opt\n  attempts at carry select, registered ALU decode, divider selection and\n  the final EX result mux did not produce an accepted gain on this parent.\n  The r14s0 timing report exposes an IF count_q-to-queue-payload path\n  through hazard/ID logic. The fixed-head FIFO computes count_q - pop\n  and decodes that index after the late consumer-stall decision. It also\n  qualifies all shifts with nonempty occupancy even though empty payload\n  contents are unobservable. Factor stall out of this control network.\nhypothesis: |\n  Change only the next-data equations of the existing four fixed-head\n  instruction FIFO payload registers. Keep binary count_q, its transition\n  logic, fetch_accept, push and pop exactly unchanged. Remove push_index\n  and the priority write/shift/hold chain. For entries i=0..3 prepare\n  held_data_i = (fetch_accept && count_q == i) ? raw_fetch : queue_q[i].\n  For entries i=0..2 also prepare\n  advanced_data_i = (fetch_accept && count_q == i+1)\n                    ? raw_fetch : queue_q[i+1].\n  Set advanced_data_3 = queue_q[3]. Clock every payload entry with\n  queue_q[i] <= stall ? held_data_i : advanced_data_i.\n  Use static generate-time indices and width-correct three-bit count\n  comparisons, ordinary ternary muxes, and no preservation attributes.\n\n  The held and advancing payload candidates depend on registered count\n  and raw readiness, not consumer stall. Stall controls only the final\n  two-input data selection. Removing the pop-dependent index arithmetic\n  and redundant nonempty qualification moves work before that late mux.\n  Keep syn_ramstyle=\\\"registers\\\", the fixed decode head, raw-response\n  fall-through, the full bundle layout and the existing output mux.\n\n  Empty, unstalled cycles may shift invalid payload bits; occupancy stays\n  zero and output continues to bypass raw_fetch. This is intentional and\n  cannot expose an instruction: refill overwrites each newly valid slot,\n  and shifting preserves the valid prefix. Nonempty queue contents and\n  all visible behavior must match the original cycle by cycle. Full\n  queues still accept no raw fetch during a pop, so tail entry 3 holds\n  when advancing. Occupancies 1..3 permit simultaneous replacement of\n  the consumed tail. When held, raw data appends at the old occupancy.\n  Reset/redirect clear occupancy with original priority; payload writes\n  remain independent of both signals, and flushed contents remain inert.\n\n  This is one local control/data-mux micro-optimization. Preserve queue\n  capacity, occupancy state, predictor and training, PC advancement and\n  recovery, FENCE.I, backend and bus stalls, instruction latency, hazard\n  equations, all execution arithmetic and forwarding. Keep nret=1, ports,\n  RVFI, illegal-instruction discipline and every contract invariant.\n\n  An exact temporary implementation passed the existing IF conservation\n  and 39 pipeline cocotb tests. Exhaustive control-equation comparison\n  passed all 80 combinations of occupancy 0..4 and ready/stall/reset/\n  redirect, checking the valid queue prefix. All eight full RVFI cosims\n  of selftest/random1/random2/random3 with ready and stalled buses passed.\n  Canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation passed with exactly\n  3984075 measured cycles. Gowin placements 0/1/2 measured\n  88.949/90.664/90.664 MHz: median 90.664 MHz, 6612 LUTs, 2801 registers,\n  zero LUT-RAM, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. This implies approximately\n  227.57 iterations/s, a 1.2 percent gain, BELOW the 4.6 percent acceptance\n  margin. The proposal makes no claim of an accepted improvement.\n\n  Predict one percent higher fitness with low confidence. Acceptance\n  requires strictly more than 235.17218 iterations/s, approximately\n  93.695 MHz at unchanged cycles. The divider recurrence remains critical\n  in placement 0, so removing queue control depth alone may not suffice.\n  A five-bit one-hot occupancy variant and a direct binary append-enable\n  variant measured only 86.912 and 86.090 MHz median; neither belongs in\n  this proposal. Do not combine these alternative implementations.\n\n  Retain all existing checks and extend the IF scoreboard to cover every\n  occupancy and control combination, checking exact ordered PC/instruction/\n  predicted_taken bundles and conservation. Compare valid queue contents,\n  not unused storage. Exercise empty shifts followed by refill, held-empty\n  capture, simultaneous push/pop, full pop with ready high, long stalls,\n  reset/redirect coincidences and existing FENCE.I refetch tests. Run the\n  unchanged formal gate, complete RVFI cosimulation, canonical stalled\n  CoreMark and all three Gowin placements during implementation evaluation.\n  Full formal has not been run during hypothesis generation and remains\n  required; no arithmetic algorithm or execution schedule changes.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 1\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove push_index and replace only the FIFO payload write/shift/hold\n      equations with the specified held and advancing data candidates\n      selected by stall at each register input. Retain binary occupancy,\n      every occupancy/PC/control equation and all existing interfaces.\n      Document that empty-queue payload shifts change only invalid storage.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing assertion and add exhaustive occupancy/control\n      transition coverage against an independent binary-count scoreboard.\n      Verify the ordered valid prefix, empty shifts followed by refill,\n      full-pop fetch suppression, simultaneous operations, conservation,\n      and reset/redirect coincidences without constraining invalid storage.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml'\nd=yaml.safe_load(open(p));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Refined YAML validates.')\nprint('Measured implied fitness:',90.664e6*10/3984075)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
