{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_71", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r8s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Compute signed and unsigned divider prefixes before mode selection'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 181.38 iterations/s at 76.245 MHz median Gowin\nFmax and 4203513 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh reproduction matches\nits 74.978/76.245 MHz placement-option-0/1 results. Option 1 is limited\nby the registered ALU operation code feeding divider remainder launch\nstate. The existing launch puts mode decoding and signed normalization\nbefore four dependent restoring steps. LESSONS.md and the r6s1/r7s1\nhistories identify this launch bottleneck, but their remedies also\nchanged multiply scheduling. Address only prefix preparation here.\nEarlier micro_opt result-mux flattening regressed; multiplier latency,\nprediction and recurrence changes are outside this hypothesis.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the real divider's four-bit launch prefix with two parallel,\nconstant combinational arithmetic networks: an unsigned prefix and a\nsigned-magnitude prefix. Select their completed eight-bit outputs with\nthe existing signed_op decode. The mode decode must enter only this\nfinal prefix selector, rather than magnitude preparation or either\nprefix calculation. This is one local divider-launch micro-optimization;\nit adds no state, execution cycle, or new instruction scheduling rule.\n\nFor the unsigned path use Nu=m_a[31:28], Du=m_b[3:0], and\nsmall_u=(m_b[31:4]==0 && m_b[3:0]\"'!=0). For the signed path compute\nNs=m_a[31] ? low4((~m_a[31:28])+(m_a[27:0]==0)) : m_a[31:28],\nand Ds=m_b[31] ? low4(0-m_b[3:0]) : m_b[3:0]. Compute\nsmall_s=(m_b[3:0]!=0) && (m_b[31] ? m_b[31:4]==28'\"'hfffffff :\nm_b[31:4]==0). These signed-path expressions depend on operand sign\nbits, never on op or signed_op. The lower-28-bit zero reduction gives\nthe carry into the leading nibble of a two's-complement magnitude.\nThis handles INT_MIN without a full-width negation in the prefix path.\n\nFor each path implement the complete function F(D,N) returning the\nfour-bit remainder followed by the four-bit quotient of N divided by D.\nFor D=0 define F(0,N)={N,4'b0}; for D=1..15 emit literal constants for\n{N modulo D, floor(N/D)}. Implement this as logic, not a 256-word ROM:\nfor each fixed divisor d and each of the eight output bits, form a\n16-bit constant truth vector indexed by N. Mask that eight-bit candidate\nwith D==d, then OR all sixteen candidates. A static generate or explicit\nblocks are suitable; each truth-vector lookup has only four inputs.\nDo not infer runtime / or %, a synchronous lookup, or a new block RAM.\nUse the complete function, without X-valued entries or approximation.\n\nCompute Pu=small_u ? F(Du,Nu) : {Nu,4'b0}, and\nPs=small_s ? F(Ds,Ns) : {Ns,4'b0}. Then prefix_pair is\nsigned_op ? Ps : Pu, retaining the existing exact signed_op expression\n(op==ALU_DIV || op==ALU_REM). The raw-small-divisor guards are essential:\nlarge divisors whose low nibble aliases a small divisor must bypass F.\nOn accepted launch initialize quotient_q to\n{dividend_magnitude[27:0],prefix_pair[3:0]} and remainder_q to\n{28'b0,prefix_pair[7:4]}. This must exactly match the current launch\nstate for every supported DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operand pair.\n\nKeep full-width dividend/divisor normalization for all other consumers,\nall registered unsigned 36-bit divisor multiples, the parallel radix-16\nrecurrence, seven busy cycles, registered completion, earliest t8 result\nconsumption, sign restoration and exceptional results unchanged. Keep\nreset cancellation, sticky completion, operand snapshots and backpressure.\nPreserve every integer and multiply operation, direct registered M inputs,\nALTOPS expressions and schedule, forwarding, predictor, memory handshakes,\nnret=1, top-level ports, decoder legality, RVFI ordering and all checks.\nOnly alu.sv and focused arithmetic tests need implementation changes.\n\nThe mechanism is removal of signed-mode decoding and a serial restoring\nprefix from the launch arithmetic. Duplicate small prefix logic costs\nLUTs but avoids replicating wide arithmetic. A preliminary single-path\nlogic-map probe reached 77.982 MHz, only 2.28 percent above the champion\nand below the acceptance threshold. Its operation decode still preceded\nthe map. The proposed two-path version moves that selection after both\ncalculations; the preliminary result does not establish its gain.\nOther probes showed that a monolithic constant case inferred a block RAM\nand regressed, while retaining serial prefix arithmetic also regressed.\nUse four-input truth vectors and explicit divisor masks as specified.\n\nPredict six-percent higher fitness with low confidence pending the full\nprobe. The recurrence and integer-result forwarding are close competing\ntiming paths, and duplicate logic or routing can erase the benefit.\nAcceptance requires strictly more than 189.72348 iterations/s, roughly\n79.751 MHz median Fmax at 4203513 cycles. Use all three vendor placement\noptions and measured marker-delimited cycles; an isolated improved path\nor a single favorable placement is insufficient.\n\nRetain all current real-arithmetic and ALTOPS tests. Exhaust all 256\nnarrow numerator/divisor pairs, signed carry boundaries with lower 28\nbits zero and nonzero, signed and unsigned +/-1..17 divisors, zero,\nINT_MIN, UINT_MAX, and large-divisor low-nibble aliases. Check exact\npost-acceptance quotient/remainder state as well as final results.\nChange live operands and op after acceptance to check snapshot isolation;\ncheck seven iterations, t8 consumption, sticky completion and reset.\nRun unchanged pipeline, formal and RVFI cosimulation checks and canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation under both bus-stall streams.\nNormal ALTOPS formal does not prove the real prefix arithmetic.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Replace only launch-prefix preparation with parallel signed-magnitude\nand unsigned four-bit truth-vector networks. Keep mode decoding out of\nboth arithmetic paths and select their guarded quotient/remainder pairs\nat the end. Preserve exact launch state, existing wide normalization,\nregistered multiples, recurrence, operation latencies and handshakes,\nall other ALU operations and the complete ALTOPS branch.\n'''\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=88));jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print('Hypothesis revised and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
