{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(s)\n if r['id']=='hyp-20261002-003-r8s2': print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Keep the current sixteen-entry agree predictor, early JAL, training timing,\nsaved-direction recovery and all pipeline cadence. Isolate predictor/branch\nresolution from the EX-to-ID producer-valid path by deriving fwd_w_en from\ninstruction class and link-write eligibility, rather than the common\nctrl_with_trap.reg_write expression. This is a single branch-resolution\nintegration change, not a different prediction policy or arithmetic unit.\n\nIn ex_stage use the equivalent reachable-state producer predicate:\nin.valid && in.ctrl.reg_write && !in.ctrl.is_branch && !misalign_jump &&\n!in.ctrl.mem_read && (!is_divide || div_result_valid).\nConditional branches are categorically non-producers before their outcome\nis resolved. JAL/JALR remain producers only when their target is aligned;\nmisaligned jumps must not forward PC+4 or write their link register. Loads\nstill cannot forward an address as data, and divides become producers only\non valid completion. Preserve x0 filtering and youngest-producer priority\nin forward_unit. Illegal instruction controls remain decoder-default inert.\n\nKeep ctrl_with_trap, misalign_fault, architectural EX/MEM.pc_next, reg_write\nat EX/MEM, branch comparison, redirect and train_valid/train_agree unchanged.\nIn particular do not globally remove branch alignment faults or change the\nregistered trap-adjusted write controls. The only disconnected dependency\nis taken-branch alignment resolution into the combinational EX forwarding\npredicate. RVFI traps, sequential trap fallback, actual successor and link\nwrite suppression remain exactly as before. No speculative result, predictor\nupdate queue, target cache, additional stage or recovery bubble is introduced.\n\nVerify the producer predicate is equivalent to the original for every\nreachable legal/illegal decoded instruction, including all six branch\nconditions and taken/not-taken aligned/misaligned targets. The proof relies\non the enforced decoder property is_branch implies !reg_write. Do not\nassume arbitrary inconsistent control bundles are architectural inputs;\nassert that decoder property explicitly instead of weakening trap checks.\nExercise adjacent consumers whose raw source numbers alias branch encoding\nrd bits, so an incorrect branch producer would corrupt forwarded operands.\n\nThe hypothesis is a timing opportunity, with expected unchanged 4203513\nCoreMark cycles. Predict five percent higher fitness with LOW confidence:\nthe divider feedback path is nearly tied with the current worst path, and\nplacement can dominate. A broader isolated probe that changed the global\nctrl_with_trap.reg_write expression passed all 30 existing pipeline tests\nbut fell to 73.778 MHz in placement 0. That probe is not the proposed change;\nkeep the registered trap controls intact and specialize only fwd_w_en.\nOther probes of registered recovery and altered predictor state also lost\nfirst-placement Fmax, so none of those changes belongs in this hypothesis.\n\nNo measured fitness improvement is claimed. At 4203513 marker-delimited\ncycles, acceptance above 181.38 * 1.046 = 189.72348 iterations/second needs\nmedian Gowin Fmax above 79.750512 MHz. Check the full paths to confirm removal\nof branch-condition logic from forwarding and run all three placements;\nreject unless measured Fmax times iterations/cycle improves over the current\nchampion by more than 4.6 percent. Preserve nret=1 and all ports, decoder\nlegality, every memory and retirement invariant, the ten-cycle branch-to-divide\nprogress bound, and real/ALTOPS M arithmetic. Run unchanged formal, pipeline\nand decoder tests, cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART validation.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
