The only disconnected dependency\nis taken-branch alignment resolution into the combinational EX forwarding\npredicate. RVFI traps, sequential trap fallback, actual successor and link\nwrite suppression remain exactly as before. No speculative result, predictor\nupdate queue, target cache, additional stage or recovery bubble is introduced.\n\nVerify the producer predicate is equivalent to the original for every\nreachable legal/illegal decoded instruction, including all six branch\nconditions and taken/not-taken aligned/misaligned targets. The proof relies\non the enforced decoder property is_branch implies !reg_write. Do not\nassume arbitrary inconsistent control bundl\n…[4394 of 7466 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7ae075e1c43c5129]…\nnt. An earlier four-byte comparator probe reached 72.526\nMHz and moved its worst reported path into queue control, so it did not\nestablish a fitness gain either. The proposed eight-nibble balanced\ntree is a different comparator topology. These negative results support\nlow confidence; do not claim a measured improvement from them.\n\nRequire equivalence of the comparator across all operand bits and legal\nbranch functions, including opposite signs and equality, then run the\nunchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates, existing unit tests, and\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker/bounded-access checks with both bus\nstall streams. Since policy and cadence are unchanged, expect exactly\n3978988 marker-delimited CoreMark cycles. Compare all three vendor\nplacement options; acceptance above 191.27 * 1.046 = 200.06842\niterations/second requires median Fmax above approximately 79.607 MHz\nat that cycle count. Preserve nret=1, all external ports, decoder\nlegality, ALTOPS/real M semantics and every existing hard invariant.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
