 [{\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_2_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.192, \"arrival_ns\": 19.486, \"logic_cells\": 19, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_10_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mult_5_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.183, \"arrival_ns\": 19.257, \"logic_cells\": 16, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_5_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mult_5_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.17, \"arrival_ns\": 19.244, \"logic_cells\": 32, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mult_5_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.168, \"arrival_ns\": 19.273, \"logic_cells\": 38, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_3_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.166, \"arrival_ns\": 19.461, \"logic_cells\": 19, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}]}]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r10s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-002-r10s1',\n'title':'Register decoded execution controls at the ID/EX boundary',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 191.27 iterations/s at 76.107 MHz and 3978988 timed\nCoreMark cycles. Prior structural gains came from changing register\nboundaries around forwarding and division. Registered multiplication\n(r6s1/r7s1) exposed divider timing limits and added dependency bubbles;\nthe radix-32 divider (r9s1) regressed. Several current probes also lost\nFmax when they changed operand storage or delayed forwarding. Instead,\nmove operation decoding across the existing ID/EX register boundary:\nALU result selection and divider launch currently decode a registered\nfive-bit operation before driving wide datapaths.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Capture a decoded execution descriptor with every ID/EX entry: fifteen\none-hot ordinary-ALU/MUL result enables, a signed-division flag and a\nremainder-selection flag. This is one structural retiming of execution\ncontrol. Keep the existing operand registers, forwarding topology,\ninstruction-stage count, arithmetic circuits and operation latencies.\n\nIn ID compute alu_select = 15'b1 << dec_alu_op, where bits 0..14 map\nexactly to ALU_ADD through ALU_MULHSU in core_pkg.sv. DIV/REM operations\n15..18 yield an all-zero ordinary-result mask. Compute divide_signed\nfor ALU_DIV/ALU_REM and divide_remainder for ALU_REM/ALU_REMU. Capture all\nthree fields inside the existing ID/EX payload update, alongside alu_op;\nreset clears them, backend_hold/load_use retain them, and redirect acts\nonly on validity. Keep alu_op for the existing execute-class detection\nand exact ALTOPS division formulas. Do not introduce a second instruction\ndecoder or relax the original default-illegal validation.\n\nFeed these registered controls into the ALU. Replace its combinational\nop-to-result case decode with fifteen mutually exclusive masked result\ncandidates and an OR reduction. Every candidate computes exactly the\ncurrent expression: ADD/SUB, logical operations, signed/unsigned compare,\nall shifts, LUI, and the four current multiply results. Compute the\narithmetic in parallel, mask each 32-bit result with its registered\none-hot bit, then combine with a balanced OR tree. All-zero selection\nreturns zero as before. Do not implement a priority case over the one-hot\nbits, add syn_keep constraints, share/replace arithmetic, or change the\nthree existing real multiply expressions. The important difference from\nr4s0's unsuccessful local result-mux rewrite is that operation decoding\nnow precedes the register boundary rather than remaining in EX.\n\nUse the registered divide_signed flag instead of decoding op in the\nreal divider's signed_op path; use divide_remainder when capturing\nwant_remainder_q. Keep full-width normalization, the narrow launch\nprefix, all registered divisor multiples, seven busy iterations, earliest\nt8 transfer, sign correction, zero-divisor override, sticky completion\nand reset cancellation unchanged. Operands remain the original direct\nregistered m_a/m_b sources. Preserve the encoded-op DIV/REM ALTOPS case\nand its exact formulas behind the unchanged controller. For the four\nmultiply result candidates, select the existing ALTOPS formulas under\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS and real products otherwise.\n\nThe expected benefit is removing post-register opcode decoding from\nordinary result selection and divider normalization/prefix launch, while\nadding only seventeen control bits before synthesis optimization. No new\nstalls or forwarding sources are introduced. The decoder-to-ID/EX path\ngets wider, and the registered one-hot controls add routing/fanout; the\nremaining branch, multiplier and divider paths can erase the benefit.\nDo not treat this as a measured gain until all three Gowin placements\nand the unchanged marker-delimited CoreMark run have been checked.\n\nPreserve nret=1, all external ports, validity-only recovery, the four-entry\nelastic fetch queue, predictor policy, memory handshakes, decoder/trap\nsemantics, exact RVFI operand/result reporting and monotonic retirement.\nRequire more than 200.06842 iterations/s for acceptance. If the expected\n3978988 timed cycles are unchanged, that requires more than 79.606984 MHz\nmedian Fmax. No evaluator or formal configuration changes are permitted.\n\nRetain all existing ALU vectors and protocol checks. Adapt standalone ALU\ntest stimulus to supply a descriptor matching op; test every operation,\nall-zero selection, signed/unsigned DIV/REM, input changes after request,\ncompletion holds and reset. Add ID/EX descriptor consistency assertions\non valid entries and verify all descriptor bits remain stable through\nbackend holds. Run existing pipeline tests, unchanged formal and full\nRVFI cosimulation with both bus-stall streams, and canonical CoreMark\nCRC/UART/marker/bounded-access validation. Real arithmetic remains covered\nindependently of ALTOPS. Update only interface/internal-layout assumptions\nin tests, preserving all architectural and progress assertions.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Extend the registered control payload with a 15-bit ALU result mask, divide_signed and divide_remainder. Keep encoded alu_op and all existing fields.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Derive the execution descriptor from the validated decoder output and capture it under the existing payload reset/hold/enable rules, independently of redirect.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Connect the registered descriptor to the ALU while retaining all operand sources, forwarding, divide handshakes, branch recovery and EX/MEM behavior.'},\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Select unchanged arithmetic results with registered one-hot masks and a balanced OR tree. Use registered division signed/remainder controls at launch. Preserve real arithmetic, ALTOPS formulas, request/result timing and exact corner cases; handle encoded op being ALTOPS-only locally for lint.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Adapt stimulus for the new decoded-control inputs without dropping arithmetic or handshake vectors. Verify every mask-to-operation mapping, zero mask, divide mode flags, holds, reset and operand isolation.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu_altops.py','description':'Supply matching registered-control descriptors in the ALTOPS harness and retain every formula, latency, backpressure and operand-isolation assertion.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Check descriptor consistency and stability through capture, load-use bubbles, backend holds and redirects. Preserve all existing source/result, memory-effect, queue, cycle-schedule and retirement assertions; adjust packed-layout helpers if necessary.'}\n]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88,default_flow_style=False))\nprint('Revised hypothesis is schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
