uest acceptance, retain the original dividend, and keep quotient and\\nremainder state in the unit. Use explicitly widened trial subtraction\\nto avoid losing the carry/borrow. Quotient sign is the operand-sign XOR;\\nremainder sign follows the dividend. Preserve divide-by-zero results\\n(all-ones quotient and original dividend r\n…[142385 of 145457 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:72444e5cb5e1979c]…\n \"vs_baseline\": 1623.93, \"fmax_mhz\": 83.245, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3984075, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6613, \"ff\": 2795, \"seeds\": [83.386, 83.245, 83.245], \"perturbations\": [[0, 83.386, 10], [1, 83.245, 9], [2, 83.245, 9]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_24_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -6.992, \"arrival_ns\": 17.287, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T12:56:34.099835Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r11s1 (improvement, +9.24%): Retiming MUL into EX/MEM and divider preparation after magnitude capture breaks both MUL-to-ID feedback and normalization-to-multiple paths; a two-bit prefix plus six radix-32 digits preserves t8 divide acceptance while MEM product forwarding confines MUL bubbles to immediate dependencies.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
