ness 126.7 fmax 56.909 cycles 4491485\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_31_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_1_s1', 'slack_ns': -12.186, 'arrival_ns': 22.48, 'logic_cells': 129, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\nhyp-20261002-002-r5s1 Replace serial divider recurrence with a parallel radix-16 digit engine fitness 152.61 fmax 68.545 cycles 4491485\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_15_s0', 'to': 'dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -10.366, 'arrival_ns': 20.661, 'logic_cells': 9, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261002-002-r6s1 Separate M-extension launch preparation from registered multiply completion fitness 159.46 fmax 73.119 cycles 4585465\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/quotient_q_0_s15', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_20_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.847, 'arrival_ns': 20.141, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu']}\nhyp-20261002-002-r7s\n…[33356 of 36428 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6de4be14cd837519]…\n Moving comparison slices\ninto ID also failed: the best full-slice probe, eight four-bit groups,\nreached 72.338 MHz median with unchanged cycles and valid CoreMark CRCs;\nasymmetric low-part retiming reached only 56.099-66.815 MHz in placement\n0. None is part of this proposal. They show why operand retiming and\ncounter recoding should not be bundled into this attempt. The proposed\nmask changes only instruction/prediction control preparation in ID.\n\nThe risk is that Gowin already folds these Boolean operations, or that\nunchanged branch-to-forwarding, divider launch and ALU-to-ID paths dominate.\nAdded mask registers and fanout can also lower Fmax. Require unchanged\nformal, full small-program RVFI cosimulation with both stall modes,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and all three vendor\nplacements. Acceptance above 191.27*1.046=200.06842 iterations/second\nrequires approximately 79.607 MHz median at the expected cycle count.\nDo not c