{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_71", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=dict(id='hyp-20261002-002-r13s1',title='Prepare PC-derived execute addresses before the ID/EX boundary',category='structural')\nd['motivation']='''The champion reaches 224.83 iterations/s at 89.575 MHz with 3984075 measured CoreMark cycles. Its recorded worst placement-0 path crosses EX branch resolution and fetch, while nearby paths include PC-derived values feeding EX result selection and ID forwarding. Earlier successful structural changes moved complete operands and memory requests across existing registers. Predictor outcome predecode and local arithmetic rewrites repeatedly failed, so this hypothesis instead moves PC-only address preparation into ID without altering prediction or branch latency.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Capture PC+4 and PC+imm alongside the existing ID/EX payload, and use these registered values for EX control-transfer endpoints and link values. This is one structural retiming of PC-derived execution addresses. It adds no pipeline stage and changes no recovery, issue, retirement or instruction latency.\n\nAdd 32-bit pc_sequential and pc_relative fields immediately after the leading pc, rs1_val and rs2_val fields of id_ex_t. In ID compute pc_sequential=in.pc+32'd4 and pc_relative=in.pc+imm from the selected IF/ID queue entry and the existing immediate generator. Capture them under exactly the existing \"'!backend_hold && !load_use payload enable, reset to zero, and retain on holds. Use full-width wrapping RV32 arithmetic. These payload computations must not depend on redirect, instruction validity or operand comparisons.\n\nIn EX replace PC+4 expressions with in.pc_sequential, including jump-link forwarding, architectural fallthrough, trap fallback, FENCE.I recovery and predicted-taken correction. Replace PC+imm expressions used by direct branch and JAL targets with in.pc_relative. Keep JALR'\"'s forwarded rs1+imm addition and low-bit clearing in EX, and preserve all alignment-fault predicates and link-write suppression. Retain the original scalar ALU's AUIPC path; do not feed AUIPC from the new relative-target field. Memory addresses, multiplication and division continue to use their existing registered operands and schedules.\n\nKeep the raw instruction PC and immediate, raw RVFI operand snapshots, branch comparisons, trap-adjusted control, train_valid/index/agree, predicted_taken association, EX advancement qualification, redirect and the fetch queue unchanged. The newly registered target contains no direction decision; target selection and architectural pc_next retain exactly their current semantics. In particular, do not postpone recovery or predictor training, add a PC-bank selector, or move operand forwarding back into EX. Preserve nret=1, the core's external ports, default-illegal decoding, all ALTOPS formulas and timing, and every hard invariant.\n\nThe intended benefit is eliminating PC adders after ID/EX from link forwarding and control-transfer target/trap paths. The ID path gains two independent PC-only adders and the payload grows by 64 bits before synthesis. Prediction and stall handling are unchanged, so expect 3984075 CoreMark cycles. Divider recurrence, added ID routing or forwarding may still dominate and erase the gain.\n\nExploratory timing of this exact two-field design measured 80.056/89.009/89.009 MHz over the three Gowin placement options, using 6580 LUTs and 2863 registers. At unchanged cycles this would be 223.411962 iterations/s, approximately 0.63 percent below the champion, so this probe has not demonstrated an improvement. Narrower variants are being evaluated before final selection. Formal has not been run. Require unchanged correctness gates, real M arithmetic, full RVFI comparisons with both bus-stall streams, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation and all three vendor placements. Acceptance requires strictly more than 235.17218 iterations/s, or 93.694361 MHz at 3984075 cycles. No evaluator, formal config, firmware or port contract changes are allowed.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':0,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add pc_sequential and pc_relative to id_ex_t after its leading PC/source-value fields, preserving all existing metadata, validity and architectural interfaces.'},{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute full-width PC+4 and PC+imm from the selected fetch bundle; capture under the existing ID/EX payload enable and retain/reset exactly like the other payload fields, independently of recovery.'},{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use the registered PC-only addresses for fallthrough, jump links, direct targets, recovery and alignment-trap reporting. Preserve the original AUIPC, JALR, memory, M-unit, forwarding, prediction-training and validity behavior.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing architectural and cycle assertions. Add checks that prepared addresses remain associated with their instruction through queue delivery, load-use/divider/dmem holds and resets; cover JAL/JALR links, AUIPC, all branch functions, taken and not-taken misaligned targets, FENCE.I, full-width wraparound, wrong-path suppression and branch-to-divide progress. Adapt packed-layout helpers only where necessary.'}]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()));print('Updated structural draft and validated schema')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
