{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_81", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Register direct control-transfer targets before execute'\nd['motivation']='''The champion reaches 224.83 iterations/s at 89.575 MHz with 3984075 measured CoreMark cycles. Its recorded worst placement-0 path crosses EX branch resolution and fetch, while nearby paths include PC-derived values feeding EX selection and ID forwarding. Successful structural changes have moved complete operands and memory requests across existing registers. Predictor outcome predecode and local arithmetic rewrites repeatedly failed. This hypothesis moves the operand-independent direct-target adder into ID, leaving its output registered before EX recovery and alignment checks.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Add one registered PC-relative target to ID/EX and use it for direct branch and JAL execution. This is a structural retiming of target-address preparation across an existing stage boundary, with no new pipeline stage, predictor policy or recovery bubble.\n\nAdd logic [31:0] pc_relative immediately after rs2_val and before imm in id_ex_t. Keep its leading pc, rs1_val and rs2_val and trailing instruction/prediction/valid metadata. In ID, capture reg_q.pc_relative <= in.pc + imm under exactly the existing \"'!backend_hold && !load_use payload enable. Use the selected IF/ID queue entry'\"'s PC and the existing imm_gen output, never the raw fetch PC. Compute this full-width wrapping sum for every payload independently of instruction validity, redirect and source operands. Reset it to zero with the bundle and retain it through backend and load-use holds.\n\nIn EX assign branch_target=in.pc_relative and use in.pc_relative for the non-JALR arm of jump_target. These are the only arithmetic substitutions. The existing redirect target selection, misaligned-target checks, branch_taken and EX/MEM.pc_next naturally consume the registered direct target. Retain the original PC+4 expressions, JALR's forwarded rs1+imm addition and low-bit clearing, and the scalar ALU's AUIPC path. Do not add a registered PC+4 field or preselect ALU operands in this hypothesis.\n\nPreserve raw PC, immediate and RVFI operands, branch comparisons, trap-adjusted write eligibility and alignment-fault behavior. A taken misaligned direct transfer still traps with the existing sequential pc_next fallback and suppresses link writes as before; a not-taken misaligned branch target does not trap. Keep control_advance, redirect qualification, train_valid/index/agree and saved predicted_taken unchanged. No direction or prediction outcome is calculated in ID. Correct prediction, recovery, FENCE.I serialization, early JAL, ordinary JALR, queue conservation and empty bypass have their exact current latency and behavior.\n\nKeep memory-request generation, load/MUL interlocks, youngest-writer forwarding, sticky divider completion, the t8 divide handshake and both real and ALTOPS arithmetic unchanged. Preserve nret=1, all top-level ports, default-illegal decoding, exact-once memory effects, architectural retirement order and every hard invariant. Contract files, firmware and evaluator configuration remain untouched.\n\nThe intended gain is removing the direct PC-plus-immediate adder from the EX target/alignment network before recovery and trap qualification. Its new ID inputs are independent of the already-long operand-forwarding path. The cost is 32 payload bits and an ID adder; synthesis may share or prune existing arithmetic. Remaining divider recurrence and ordinary ALU-to-ID feedback limit the headroom.\n\nA temporary implementation of this exact single-target retiming measured 79.666/91.786/91.786 MHz across Gowin placement options 0/1/2, using 6599 LUTs, 2833 registers, zero LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. At the expected unchanged 3984075 measured cycles, the median implies approximately 230.384 iterations/s, about 2.47 percent above the recorded champion. This is the strongest structural probe from this session, but it does NOT demonstrate the required 4.6 percent acceptance margin. Predict two percent higher fitness with low confidence rather than claiming acceptance. Formal has not been run on the probe and remains required.\n\nPreparing both PC+4 and PC+imm reached only 89.009 MHz median; PC+4 alone reached 87.723 MHz. Registering both ALU operands reached 85.783 MHz. A separate recovery-PC bank preserving cycle latency reached 85.522 MHz, and delaying recovery by one cycle reached 77.794 MHz while raising CoreMark cycles to 4052921. These alternatives are excluded from the proposal. Do not bundle them with direct-target retiming.\n\nRequire the unchanged formal gate, existing unit assertions, real M arithmetic, full small-program RVFI comparisons under ready and stalled buses, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks, and all three vendor placements. Expected marker-delimited CoreMark cycles are 3984075. Acceptance requires strictly more than 235.17218 iterations/s, or 93.694361 MHz at that cycle count. Record the actual measured result even if the candidate remains below the acceptance threshold.'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':2,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add the 32-bit pc_relative field to id_ex_t immediately after rs2_val and before imm, preserving existing instruction/prediction/valid metadata and the external single-retirement contract.'},{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Capture full-width in.pc+imm in pc_relative under the existing ID/EX payload enable. Use the selected queue-entry PC, reset and retain the field with the rest of the bundle, and keep target preparation independent of redirect, validity and forwarded operands.'},{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace only branch_target=in.pc+in.imm and the direct-JAL jump_target arm with in.pc_relative. Preserve PC+4, AUIPC, JALR, alignment traps, target selection, branch direction, recovery/training cadence, RVFI successors and all forwarding and memory behavior.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain every existing architectural and cycle assertion; add prepared-target association checks across queue delivery, load-use/divider/dmem holds and resets. Cover direct jumps, JALR and AUIPC non-regression, all branch functions, taken/not-taken misaligned targets, FENCE.I, full-width target wraparound, wrong-path suppression and branch-to-divide progress. Adjust layout-aware helpers only as required.'}]\nclass LiteralDumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nLiteralDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=LiteralDumper,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Schema valid; projected fitness',91.786*1e7/3984075)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
