{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ns=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/186fdfda/headtail_binary.sv').read_text()\ns=s.replace('tail_q [0:2]', 'tail_q [0:1]').replace('logic [1:0] tail_read_q, tail_write_q;', 'logic tail_read_q, tail_write_q;').replace(\\\"count_q \"'!= 3'\"'d4\\\", \\\"count_q \"'!= 3'\"'d3\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"tail_read_q <= 2'b0\\\", \\\"tail_read_q <= 1'b0\\\").replace(\\\"tail_write_q <= 2'b0\\\", \\\"tail_write_q <= 1'b0\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"tail_read_q <= tail_read_q == 2'd2 ? 2'd0 : tail_read_q + 2'd1\\\", \\\"tail_read_q <= \"'!tail_read_q\").replace(\"tail_write_q <= tail_write_q == 2'\"'d2 ? 2'd0 : tail_write_q + 2'd1\\\", \\\"tail_write_q <= \"'!tail_write_q\")\nPath('\"'cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv').write_text(s)\nPY\nNRET=1 make cosim-build TARGET=bench > cores/bench/headtail_three_build_r15.log 2>&1\ncores/bench/obj_dir/cosim_sim bench/programs/coremark.elf 50000000 --bench --istall --dstall > cores/bench/headtail_three_coremark_r15.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_81", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r15s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Use a dedicated decode head with a two-slot circular fetch tail'\nd['motivation']='''The four-entry shift FIFO hides fetch stalls, but vendor paths cross its occupancy, hazard and insertion-control loop. A registered decode head with a circular tail preserves the short decode read path. Four-entry prototypes measured 88.650 MHz with binary tail pointers and 88.842 MHz with one-hot occupancy, below the 89.575 MHz champion. The proposed three-entry structure instead uses a two-slot tail: one-bit pointers, a two-way head-refill mux and one fewer full instruction bundle. This targets queue control and routing cost while retaining empty bypass and fetch/backend overlap.'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Restructure instruction buffering as one dedicated decode-head register and two circular tail registers, for total capacity three. This is a single structural fetch-queue hypothesis. Preserve single issue, nret=1, the predictor, raw empty bypass and the existing execution pipeline. The selected tail data feeds only the head register at an edge; decode sees the registered head or the existing raw empty bypass, never a pointer-selected tail read.\n\nRetain count_q with its current three-bit width so existing observations remain available, but restrict occupancy to 0..3. Define fetch_accept = imem_ready && count_q \"'!= 3; pop = count_q != 0 && !stall; push = fetch_accept && (count_q != 0 || stall). Update count by +1 on push only, -1 on pop only, and hold on both/neither. A full queue rejects the raw response even on a simultaneous pop and resumes fetching next cycle, keeping capacity independent of combinational decode-ready. Advance the fetch PC only on fetch_accept, with the existing reset/redirect priority and predictor.\n\nStore complete if_id_t bundles in one head_q and two flop-backed tail_q entries. On push into an empty queue, capture raw_fetch into head_q. On pop with old count greater than one, refill head_q from tail_q[tail_read_q]. On pop with old count equal to one and fetch_accept, replace the head directly with raw_fetch. Otherwise retain the head payload. A consumed raw empty bypass is not enqueued.\n\nUse one-bit tail_read_q and tail_write_q pointers. Define tail_pop = pop && count_q > 1 and tail_push = push && (count_q > 1 || (count_q == 1 && !pop)). Write raw_fetch into the selected tail slot only on tail_push. Toggle each pointer only on its corresponding tail transfer. Reset and redirect clear count and both pointers. No modulo-three arithmetic or three-way read mux remains. Old-state reads on simultaneous tail transfers preserve FIFO order. At count one, simultaneous pop/push replaces only the head and moves neither pointer. At count three, raw acceptance is inhibited, so a full-tail pop cannot collide with a same-slot push.\n\nRemove the shifting queue entries, count-minus-pop insertion arithmetic and shift/append arbitration. Force flop storage as in the existing queue. Payload writes need no recovery/reset gating: occupancy and reset pointers invalidate flushed entries. Keep each saved instruction, PC, valid and predicted_taken together. Preserve recovery during imem stalls, deferred EX recovery during older dmem holds, predictor training cadence and FENCE.I flushing.\n\nChange no ALU, forwarding, divider, multiplier, memory handshake or retirement behavior. Preserve nret=1, top-level ports, decoder legality, traps, all hard invariants and all protected files. Do not combine this proposal with AUIPC retiming or arithmetic changes.\n\nThe tradeoff is a smaller queue, which can increase fetch-empty cycles, in exchange for simpler control, less movement and lower storage/routing cost. Unlike the four-entry probes, the tail has power-of-two depth and only a two-way refill mux. Predict a six-percent fitness improvement with low confidence; the final three-entry proposal has no completed vendor timing measurement and has not demonstrated acceptance. Judge actual median Fmax times measured iterations/cycle, including the smaller queue'\"'s cycle cost. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 235.17218 iterations/s.\n\nRun lint, an adapted independent FIFO conservation model, existing architectural pipeline checks, full RVFI cosimulation under ready/stalled buses, the unchanged formal gate, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and all three Gowin placements. Update only occupancy/capacity-dependent timing expectations to capacity three; preserve all exact-once, ordering, operand, trap and bounded-progress assertions. Formal proof remains required.'''\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Replace four shifting entries with a dedicated head and two circular flop tail entries. Use one-bit read/write pointers, total capacity three, the specified transfer conditions, unchanged empty bypass and predictor/PC/flush behavior. Remove push_index and wide tail shifting. Keep count_q observable for tests.'},{'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'Adapt the independent FIFO/predictor model from capacity four to capacity three without weakening conservation or ordering. Cover all occupancies 0..3, full backpressure, repeated tail wraps, simultaneous refill/append, count-one direct replacement, every pointer position, reset, redirects and imem stalls.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve architectural assertions and execution-stage latency expectations. Adapt only fetch-capacity-dependent checks. Exercise tail wrap across load/MUL dependencies, divider waits, long dmem holds, branch recovery and FENCE.I. Check instruction/PC/prediction association, exact-once memory effects, monotonic retirement and wrong-path suppression.'}]\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=95))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final three-entry proposal is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
