{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261002-002-r1s1|divider|pipeline' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share DIV and REM through a fused-subtract unsigned divider\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns worst path spanning forwarding and the EX ALU\\nwith 156 cells. There are no prior divider experiments or LESSONS.md.\\nalu.sv independently expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder\\nwith / and %, leaving arithmetic sharing and divider topology to Gowin.\\nTheir deep combinational logic is the strongest RTL-level explanation for\\nthis path, though the available path summary does not identify an operator.\\nA smaller, explicitly shared divider with one subtract/borrow decision per\\nquotient bit can improve the clock period without costing CoreMark cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns worst path spanning forwarding and the EX ALU\\nwith 156 cells. There are no prior divider experiments or LESSONS.md.\\nalu.sv independently expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder\\nwith / and %, leaving arithmetic sharing and divider topology to Gowin.\\nTheir deep combinational logic is the strongest RTL-level explanation for\\nthis path, though the available path summary does not identify an operator.\\nA smaller, explicitly shared divider with one subtract/borrow decision per\\nquotient bit can improve the clock period without costing CoreMark cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one combinational\\nunsigned restoring divider that produces both quotient and remainder.\\nFor DIV and REM, convert operands to unsigned two's-complement magnitudes;\\nfor DIVU and REMU, use the original unsigned operands. Restore the quotient\\nsign from a[31] XOR b[31], and the remainder sign from a[31], only for the\\nsigned operations. Select quotient versus remainder after the shared core.\\n\\nImplement the divider as 32 statically unrolled, progres\n…[25379 of 28451 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a5cc11601976a4e1]…\nnt.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 13.12, \"delta_pct\": 8.25, \"vs_baseline\": 8.25, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.514, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201709, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12959, \"ff\": 621, \"seeds\": [5.203, 5.514, 5.514], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.203, 152], [1, 5.514, 154], [2, 5.514, 154]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -187.195, \"arrival_ns\": 197.49, \"logic_cells\": 160, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 152, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T05:59:14.786124Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.25%): A 64-entry BHT plus early JAL cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.45% at nearly unchanged Fmax (5.514 MHz), but lost to iterative division because prediction left the combinational DIV/REM timing bottleneck intact.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
