      Ensure backend holds preserve complete operands and load-use keeps\n      its current bubble timing. Document the earlier forwarding boundary.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Consume captured ID/EX sources directly for all execution and RVFI\n      paths. Export the current architectural result and valid,\n      trap-adjusted producer eligibility to ID; exclude EX loads and use\n      PC+4 for jumps and completed results for divides. Preserve divider\n      control, alignment traps, branch timing and EX/MEM hold behavior.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Export the existing load-extraction result or registered ALU value,\n      plus valid trap-adjusted write eligibility, for early operand capture.\n      Preserve byte lanes, memory handshakes, misalignment suppression,\n      retained WB payload and exact-once retirement unchanged.\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Use explicit flop storage, or the demonstrated Gowin registers\n      inference attribute, to preserve an independent ID/EX operand\n      capture boundary. Keep both asynchronous read ports, synchronous\n      writes, complete reset semantics, x0 and WB write-first behavior.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add youngest-writer priority tests with EX, MEM and WB targeting\n      the same source, both operand ports, x0 and rd/source overlap.\n      Exercise ALU/MUL/jump-link forwarding, load-use with byte/halfword\n      extension, divider completion to an immediate consumer, and stalled\n      branches/stores retaining captured values after producers drain.\n      Include simultaneous bus stalls, wrong-path instructions, invalid\n      producer payloads and misaligned jump/load producers that must not\n      forward. Check exact RVFI sources/results/PC/order and exact-once\n      memory effects. Retain all arithmetic and liveness checks.\n'''\np.write_text(s)\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nv=yaml.safe_load(s);jsonschema.validate(v,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));print('Revised structural hypothesis is schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu_altops.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\nRevised structural hypothesis is schema-valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r4s1.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
