t acceptance, retain the original dividend, and keep quotient and\\nremainder state in the unit. Use explicitly widened trial subtraction\\nto avoid losing the carry/borrow. Quotient sign is the operand-sign XOR;\\nremainder sign follows the dividend. Preserve divide-by-zero results\\n(all-ones quotient and original dividend r\n…[65811 of 68883 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b56df7723809b8b7]…\nipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4654, \"ff\": 1901, \"seeds\": [65.078, 68.545, 68.545], \"perturbations\": [[0, 65.078, 9], [1, 68.545, 9], [2, 68.545, 9]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_15_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -10.366, \"arrival_ns\": 20.661, \"logic_cells\": 9, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 9, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T08:22:20.812597Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r5s1 (improvement, +20.45%): Registered unsigned 36-bit divisor multiples, parallel radix-16 subtractors and balanced one-hot selection replace four serial restoring subtract/select chains in the divider feedback path, raising median Fmax from 56.909 to 68.545 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles and moving the bottleneck to ordinary EX arithmetic/result selection.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
