{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_96", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r6s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Separate M-extension launch preparation from registered multiply completion'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 152.61 iterations/s at 68.545 MHz and 4491485\nmarker-delimited CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at\nID/EX rs2_val[15], passes through EX arithmetic/result selection, and\nends at dmem, with 20.661 ns arrival time. LESSONS.md and the structural\nhistory show that early operand capture and the parallel radix-16\nrecurrence removed earlier bottlenecks. The r4s1 multiplier-only probe\nfailed while other paths dominated. A fresh multiplier-only probe on\nthis champion also failed: the divider's launch normalization/prefix\nbecame critical and median Fmax fell to 57.299 MHz. The promising\nstructural angle is therefore to isolate M-extension arithmetic at its\nlaunch/completion boundaries, addressing the exposed launch dependency\nas part of moving multiplication out of single-cycle EX.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Separate M-extension launch preparation and completed-result delivery\nfrom the ordinary single-cycle execute path. Give MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU\na registered product boundary, and make the existing divider's narrow\nlaunch prefix independent of full-width magnitude normalization. This\nis one structural redesign of the M-unit timing boundaries. It changes\nneither the instruction pipeline depth nor the existing divide schedule.\nBoth parts are necessary: the isolated multiplier and isolated prefix\nprobes below each lose to the champion.\n\nLaunch multiplication directly from fully forwarded ID/EX rs1 and rs2,\nwithout the AUIPC/immediate operand muxes. Form one signed 33-by-33\nproduct: extend A with its sign for MULH/MULHSU and zero otherwise;\nextend B with its sign for MULH and zero otherwise. Explicitly cast\nboth operands to signed 33-bit values and capture a signed 66-bit\nproduct plus a high/low selector at request edge t0. After this register,\nselect bits 31:0 for MUL or 63:32 for the three high-half operations.\nThis gives exact signed/unsigned results without serial high-half sign\ncorrection. Remove the active combinational MUL paths from the ordinary\nALU result. The first possible EX/MEM acceptance is t1, costing one\nextra cycle per multiply except where an older memory hold hides it.\n\nUse a single-outstanding request/completion protocol. EX launches a\nvalid legal multiply exactly once, holds PC and ID/EX through the\nexisting execute_wait interlock, and lets older stages drain. Once an\nolder EX/MEM entry advances, emit invalid bubbles while waiting; retain\nan older stalled memory request under the existing dmem hold instead.\nA multiply may launch during that hold because its captured source\nvalues are complete. Retain product, selector and completion until\nEX/MEM accepts them, then consume exactly once. Reset cancels pending\nwork. Forward only completed products, including to a dependent ID\ncapture on the completion transfer edge. Preserve source snapshots,\nx0, producer age priority, trap eligibility and exact RVFI retirement.\nKeep multiply and divide completion state independent so consecutive\nand mixed M operations cannot consume the wrong result.\n\nThe divider launch must not serialize a 32-bit absolute value into four\nrestoring prefix steps. Keep full-width magnitude generation for the\nquotient's lower bits and registered divisor multiples, but prepare the\nleading nibble and small-divisor decision in parallel from raw ALU\noperands A and B. Let negA = signed_op && A[31], and likewise negB,\nwhere signed_op identifies DIV/REM. Compute the four-bit leading\nmagnitude nibble N as A[31:28] when positive, or\n(~A[31:28] + (A[27:0] == 0)) modulo 16 when negative. The lower-bit\nzero reduction supplies the only carry needed by this high nibble.\nCompute four-bit D as B[3:0], or -B[3:0] modulo 16 when negB.\nThe exact nonzero-small-divisor predicate is B[3:0] \"'!= 0 and either\nall B[31:4] bits equal one when negB, or all equal zero otherwise.\nThus magnitudes 1..15 are recognized without a 32-bit negate/comparison;\nzero and magnitude 16 or larger never enter the small-divisor path.\n\nReplace the four dependent restoring-prefix cells with a complete\ncombinational 256-entry, eight-bit constant map keyed by {D,N}.\nFor D=1..15, the output is {N modulo D, floor(N/D)}, each four bits.\nFor D=0 define it as {N,4'\"'b0}; the existing zero-divisor result override\nremains authoritative. Emit literal constants in a complete case table,\nnot runtime division or remainder operators. On request acceptance,\ninitialize quotient_q to {dividend_magnitude[27:0], small ? Q4 : 4'b0}\nand remainder_q to {28'b0, small ? R4 : N}. Preserve the existing\nregistered 36-bit divisor multiples, seven subsequent radix-16\niterations, earliest t8 result handshake, sign correction, sticky\ncompletion and all division corner cases. Large divisors must not be\ntruncated into the lookup. Keep portable combinational semantics if\nGowin infers a ROM and absorbs the existing capture register; do not\nadd a ROM cycle or use vendor-only primitives.\n\nUnder RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, capture the existing exact MUL-family XOR\nformulas behind the same new request/wait/completion timing. Keep the\nexisting division ALTOPS formulas and divider controller schedule.\nPreserve nret=1, every core port, decoder legality, alignment traps,\nregister-file mapping, validity-only recovery, memory handshakes and\nall hard invariants. No predictor, cache, extra instruction stage or\nother architectural change is part of this hypothesis.\n\nA temporary combined RTL probe passed Verilator lint, eight full RVFI\ntrace comparisons (selftest and random1/2/3, each with ready buses and\nwith both stall modes), and the canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/\nmarker checks without out-of-bounds accesses. CoreMark took 4585465\nmeasured cycles, 2.09 percent more than the champion. Gowin placement\noptions 0/1/2 reached 72.133/73.509/73.509 MHz, giving a 73.509 MHz\nmedian and estimated fitness 160.3087, 5.0447 percent above 152.61.\nArea was 4551 LUTs, 1919 flip-flops, five BSRAMs and two DSPs. The\nworst reported path moved into the divider recurrence. A multiplier-only\nablation gave 57.299 MHz and the same 4585465 cycles; prefix-only gave\n67.051 MHz. These measurements support the combined M-unit boundary\nchange rather than either isolated edit. They are exploratory probe\nresults, not an accepted evaluation; formal and formal-deep were not run.\n\nPredict 5 percent higher fitness with medium confidence. Acceptance\nrequires fitness above 159.63006, or median Fmax above 73.197806 MHz at\n4585465 cycles. The measured margin is narrow, so reproduce all three\nplacements and marker cycles after implementation. Verify real MUL and\nDIV arithmetic, prefix initialization at signed carry boundaries,\ncompletion retention, reset and dependencies using the existing suites\nplus directed cases. Run every unchanged formal/cosimulation/CoreMark\ngate; ALTOPS does not prove the new real multiplier or prefix datapath.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Add a direct-source multiply request/completion interface, shared\nsigned 33-by-33 multiplication, registered 66-bit product and selector,\nand sticky completion. Remove active combinational MUL output paths\nand preserve exact ALTOPS formulas behind the new latency. In the same\nM-unit launch redesign, derive the dividend magnitude's high nibble,\ndivisor low nibble and small-divisor predicate directly from raw\noperands, and replace serial launch-prefix steps with the complete\n256-entry constant quotient/remainder case table. Preserve full-width\nmagnitudes/multiples, seven divider iterations, t8 consumption,\ncorrection, corner cases and every ordinary integer operation.\n'''\nd['changes'][2]['description']+='''\nAdd all 256 prefix lookup combinations and launch-state comparisons\nfor both signed and unsigned operations. Cover every dividend high\nnibble with low 28 bits zero, one and all ones; positive and negative\ndivisors of magnitude 1..17; zero, INT_MIN and large divisors whose low\nnibble aliases a small divisor. Check exact initialized quotient and\nremainder as well as final results and unchanged t8 timing.\n'''\nclass LiteralDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nLiteralDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=LiteralDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261002-002-r6s1' and d['category']=='structural'\nprint('Revised hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
