oth stall modes), and the canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/\nmarker checks without out-of-bounds accesses. CoreMark took 4585465\nmeasured cycles, 2.09 percent more than the champion. Gowin placement\noptions 0/1/2 reached 72.133/73.509/73.509 MHz, giving a 73.509 MHz\nmedian and estimated fitness 160.3087, 5.0447 percent above 152.61.\nArea was 4551 LUTs, 1919 flip-flops, five BSRAMs and two DSPs. The\nworst reported path moved into the divider recurrence. A multiplier-only\nablation gave 57.299 MHz and the same 4585465 cycles; prefix-only gave\n67.051 MHz. These measurements support the combined M-unit boundary\nchange rather than either isolated edit. They are exploratory probe\nresults, not an accepted evaluation; formal and formal-deep were not run.\n\nPredict 5 percent higher fitness with medium confidence. Acceptance\nrequires fitness above 159.63006, or median Fmax above 73.197806 MHz at\n4585465 cycles. The measured margin is narrow, so reproduce all three\nplacements and marker cycles after implementation. Verify real MUL and\nDIV arithmetic, prefix initialization at signed carry boundaries,\ncompletion retention, reset and dependencies using the existing suites\nplus directed cases. Run every unchanged formal/cosimulation/CoreMark\ngate; ALTOPS does not prove the new real multiplier or prefix datapath.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Add a direct-source multiply request/completion interface, shared\nsigned 33-by-33 multiplication, registered 66-bit product and selector,\nand sticky completion. Remove active combinational MUL output paths\nand preserve exact ALTOPS formulas behind the new latency. In the same\nM-unit launch redesign, derive the dividend magnitude's high nibble,\ndivisor low nibble and small-divisor predicate directly from raw\noperands, and replace serial launch-prefix steps with the complete\n256-entry constant quotient/remainder case table. Preserve full-width\nmagnitudes/multiples, seven divider iterations, t8 consumption,\ncorrection, corner cases and every ordinary integer operation.\n'''\nd['changes'][2]['description']+='''\nAdd all 256 prefix lookup combinations and launch-state comparisons\nfor both signed and unsigned operations. Cover every dividend high\nnibble with low 28 bits zero, one and all ones; positive and negative\ndivisors of magnitude 1..17; zero, INT_MIN and large divisors whose low\nnibble aliases a small divisor. Check exact initialized quotient and\nremainder as well as final results and unchanged t8 timing.\n'''\nclass LiteralDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nLiteralDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=LiteralDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261002-002-r6s1' and d['category']=='structural'\nprint('Revised hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised hypothesis written and schema-valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
