{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261002-002-r[678]s1|worst_path|MUL' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move DIV/REM into a shared iterative execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 CoreMark iterations/s,\\n5.442 MHz median Fmax, and 12,312 LUT4s. Its worst path takes 199.837 ns\\nthrough forwarding and the execute ALU, with 156 cells. The ALU implements\\nsigned and unsigned division and remainder as combinational / and %.\\nThese operators are a strong explanation for the deep arithmetic path:\\neven instructions that do not divide pay its clock-period cost. There is\\nno LESSONS.md and no prior structural attempt in the available log.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 CoreMark iterations/s,\\n5.442 MHz median Fmax, and 12,312 LUT4s. Its worst path takes 199.837 ns\\nthrough forwarding and the execute ALU, with 156 cells. The ALU implements\\nsigned and unsigned division and remainder as combinational / and %.\\nThese operators are a strong explanation for the deep arithmetic path:\\neven instructions that do not divide pay its clock-period cost. There is\\nno LESSONS.md and no prior structural attempt in the available log.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU circuits with one shared,\\nbounded-latency iterative divider inside alu.sv. Keep integer operations\\nand multiplication on their existing execution paths. This is one\\nstructural change: separate variable-latency division from ordinary EX.\\n\\nUse unsigned restoring division with four quotient bits computed per\\ncycle by four explicitly bounded shift/subtract/select steps, for eight\\niteration cycles. Register the normalized operands and signedness at\\nrequest acceptance, retain the original dividend, and keep quotient and\\nremainder state in the unit. Use explicitly widened trial subtraction\\nto avoid losing the carry/borrow. Quotient sign is the operand-sign XOR;\\nremainder sign follows the dividend. Preserve divide-by-zero results\\n(all-ones quotient and original dividend r\n…[127004 of 130076 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a5d89e7f354c29e0]…\n\": 5.45, \"vs_baseline\": 1478.14, \"fmax_mhz\": 76.107, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3978988, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5106, \"ff\": 2209, \"seeds\": [73.244, 76.107, 76.107], \"perturbations\": [[0, 73.244, 11], [1, 76.107, 10], [2, 76.107, 10]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.is_auipc_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_uu_63_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -8.653, \"arrival_ns\": 18.727, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T10:58:20.170887Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r8s1 (improvement, +5.45%): A four-entry fixed-head flop FIFO with empty bypass overlaps fetch with load-use, divider and dmem holds to reduce CoreMark cycles, while its fixed decode head and bypass avoid the timing and latency penalties seen in circular-queue and no-bypass probes.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
