0.326 CYC 4491485\nhyp-20261002-002-r4s1 structural Resolve forwarding before the ID/EX operand registers FIT 126.7 FMAX 56.909 CYC 4491485\nhyp-20261002-003-r4s2 predictor A 16-entry agree predictor with validity-only recovery FIT 115.14 FMAX 48.401 CYC 4203513\nhyp-20261002-001-r5s0 micro_opt Shorten the isolated divider recurrence with parallel radix-4 digits FIT 128.02 FMAX 57.5 CYC 4491485\nhyp-20261002-002-r5s1 structural Replace serial divider recurrence with a parallel radix-16 digit engine FIT 152.61 FMAX 68.545 CYC 4491485\nhyp-20261002-003-r5s2 predictor Compact agree prediction with registered EX operands FIT 136.72 FMAX 57.47 CYC 4203513\nhyp-20261002-0\n…[24439 of 27511 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:70ff238e203f9c1c]…\nnonzero, signed and unsigned +/-1..17 divisors, zero,\nINT_MIN, UINT_MAX, and large-divisor low-nibble aliases. Check exact\npost-acceptance quotient/remainder state as well as final results.\nChange live operands and op after acceptance to check snapshot isolation;\ncheck seven iterations, t8 consumption, sticky completion and reset.\nRun unchanged pipeline, formal and RVFI cosimulation checks and canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation under both bus-stall streams.\nNormal ALTOPS formal does not prove the real prefix arithmetic.\n\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_uu_63_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.746, 'arrival_ns': 19.851, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\nhyp-20261002-002-r8s1 structural Decouple fetch with a fixed-head elastic instruction queue FIT 191.27 FMAX 76.107 CYC 3978988\nhyp-20261002-003-r8s2 predictor Isolate branch-predictor resolution from EX forwarding eligibility FIT 155.78 FMAX 65.483 CYC 4203513\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
