{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r9s1.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-002-r9s1',\n 'title':'Replace divider launch-prefix work with seven uniform radix-32 iterations',\n 'category':'structural',\n 'motivation':'''The current champion scores 191.27 iterations/s at 76.107 MHz and\n3978988 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Prior structural successes removed\nserial divider depth and registered its completion; r6s1/r7s1 multiplier\npipelines instead exposed divider launch/recurrence limits. The current\nlaunch edge normalizes operands, builds divisor multiples, and performs\nfour serial narrow restoring steps. The r8s0 prefix-only rewrite reached\n76.371 MHz and did not clear acceptance. Change the divider's work\nschedule so launch does no quotient selection, retaining the proven\nregistered completion and unchanged t8 acceptance time.\n''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace the launch-prefix plus seven radix-16 iterations with launch\nnormalization plus seven uniform radix-32 iterations. This is one\nstructural redesign of the divider's digit width and register boundaries.\nRetain the existing request/busy/done controller, seven busy edges,\nearliest t8 result handshake and sticky completion. Keep the integer\npipeline, combinational multiplication, forwarding, four-entry elastic\nfetch queue, predictor and all memory/retirement interfaces unchanged.\n\nOn accepted launch capture the original dividend, signedness, quotient\nand remainder signs, desired result kind, zero-divisor flag and normalized\nunsigned divisor. Initialize a 35-bit quotient register to the 32-bit\nunsigned dividend magnitude with three leading zero bits; initialize the\n32-bit remainder to zero. Remove small_divisor qualification and every\nprefix quotient/remainder calculation. Preserve full-width normalization,\nincluding the magnitude of INT_MIN, and request-time operand snapshots.\n\nCapture widened divisor multiples 1D through 31D on this same edge. Use\n37 unsigned bits throughout: 31*UINT_MAX fits, and all five incoming bits\nmust participate in the borrow decision. Reuse the divisor register for\n1D. For each multiple, factor powers of two out of its index. Generate\nodd multiples with shifts, one add/subtract for two-term constants, and\ncarry-save compression followed by one carry-propagating addition for\nthree/four-term constants. Avoid cascades of full-width carry-propagating\nadders. Three-input compression computes P=X xor Y xor Z and\nC=((X&Y)|(X&Z)|(Y&Z))<<1, then P+C. Compress a fourth term in a second\ncarry-save layer before the final addition. For 23D, use 16D+8D-D:\ncompress X=16D, Y=8D, Z=~D in 37 bits, then add P to (C|1);\nC bit zero is known zero, so the one supplies two's-complement carry-in.\nUse direct shift/subtract for 7D, 15D and 31D. All expressions are exact\nmodulo 2\"'^37, which equals the full nonnegative result in this range.\nKeep this portable synthesizable logic, with no runtime / or %, vendor\nprimitive, inferred ROM, extra normalization cycle, or new ALTOPS formula.\n\nAt each of seven busy edges form T={remainder_q,quotient_q[34:30]}.\nCompute all 31 independent widened subtractions {0,T}-{0,kD} in\n38 bits. success[k] is the inverse borrow bit. Select digit zero when\nsuccess[1] is false, digit k for success[k] && !success[k+1], and digit\n31 when success[31] is true. Form 32 mutually exclusive 37-bit candidates\ncontaining {selected_remainder[31:0],digit[4:0]} and combine them with an\nexplicit balanced 32-to-16-to-8-to-4-to-2-to-1 masked-OR tree. Capture\nquotient_q={quotient_q[29:0],digit} and remainder_q=selected_remainder.\nFor nonzero D, R<D implies T<32D, making each selected digit exact and\nthe new remainder fit 32 bits. Starting with three leading zeros means\nseven five-bit shifts process precisely the 32 dividend bits; the first\ndigit consumes only two nonzero-capable source bits. The final quotient\nis quotient_q[31:0], with its upper three bits zero for nonzero divisors.\n\nOnly completed quotient/remainder registers feed the existing sign and\nzero-divisor correction. Preserve all-ones DIV/DIVU by zero, original\nbit-pattern REM/REMU by zero, INT_MIN/-1 quotient and zero remainder,\nsigned truncation and remainder sign. Zero-divisor recurrence may select\n31, but the registered architectural override remains authoritative.\nKeep real and ALTOPS request/wait/result timing identical, retaining every\nexisting ALTOPS XOR formula. Reset cancels pending work; completion freezes\nuntil consumed; never forward an intermediate quotient or replay a divide.\n\nA temporary radix-32 probe with ordinary shift/add/subtract multiples\npassed lint, the existing pipeline suite, selftest RVFI comparison with\nready and stalled buses, and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/\nmarker validation. CoreMark retained exactly 3978988 timed cycles.\nGowin placements 0/1/2 measured 77.405/78.538/78.538 MHz, using 6598 LUTs,\n2733 registers, zero LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and six DSPs. That is only about\n3.2 percent higher fitness, below acceptance. Timing still includes\nnormalization into complex divisor multiples; carry-save generation is\nthe concrete refinement proposed here. Its timing is not yet established.\nDo not claim the preliminary probe cleared the tournament threshold.\n\nPredict six percent higher fitness with low confidence until the refined\nvendor measurements complete. The wider bank and 32-way selection increase\nrouting and fanout, and ordinary EX feedback can still cap Fmax. Acceptance\nrequires strictly more than 200.06842 iterations/s, or 79.606984 MHz median\nFmax at unchanged cycles. Measure all three placements and the actual\nmarker-delimited cycles. Preserve nret=1, core ports, every hard invariant\nand all evaluation files. Run unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates;\nALTOPS formal alone does not establish the new real arithmetic.\n\nAdapt internal arithmetic-state assertions to a 35-bit initial quotient,\nzero initial remainder and five-bit recurrence without removing any\nexisting operand vector or architectural assertion. Extend the existing\narbitrary-R<D recurrence test from 16 to all 32 digit possibilities,\ncheck all 31 registered multiples, boundaries kD-1/kD/kD+1, maximum\n37-bit trials, and large divisors. Retain signed/unsigned corner cases,\nzero division, input changes after launch, seven busy edges, t8 acceptance,\nlong completion backpressure, reset cancellation and all pipeline hazards.\n'\"''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Replace the launch prefix/radix-16 engine with a 35-bit dividend/quotient,\nzero-remainder initialization and seven radix-32 digits. Capture exact\n37-bit multiples 1..31 using carry-save constant-product preparation;\nuse full 38-bit borrow decisions and balanced one-hot digit selection.\nPreserve request/completion timing, sign/exception semantics, snapshots,\nreset, integer/MUL datapaths and the exact ALTOPS branch/controller.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Preserve all arithmetic vectors and external protocol checks. Update\ninternal state models for 35-bit quotient, zero-prefix launch and five-bit\ndigits. Extend multiple-bank checks to 31D and recurrence assertions to\nall 32 digits, boundary trials and 37-bit intermediates. Verify original\nsigned/unsigned results, input isolation, holds, reset and exact t8 timing.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_alu_altops.py','description':'''Retain every existing exact ALTOPS formula and timing assertion. Confirm\nthat real-engine restructuring has not changed launch, seven busy cycles,\ncompletion retention, ready/valid behavior or operand isolation.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing forwarding, queue, branch, memory and RVFI check.\nAdd full-width division cases spanning radix-32 digit boundaries through\ndependent ALU/branch/store consumers, consecutive divides, x0 and older\nstalled memory. Require unchanged execution schedule, exact operands and\nresults, no wrong-path effects, monotonic retirement and bounded progress.'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Revised and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
