{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r9s1.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());h=d['hypothesis']\na=h.index('Capture widened odd divisor multiples');b=h.index('At each of seven busy edges',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''Capture widened divisor multiples 1D through 31D at launch in a full\nregistered bank. Use 37 unsigned bits throughout: 31*UINT_MAX fits and\nall five incoming bits participate in each borrow decision. Reuse the\nnormalized divisor register for 1D. Generate each constant product from\nat most three signed power-of-two terms with explicitly widened shifts,\nadds and subtracts, registering the full product independently. Use a\ncanonical signed-digit expansion: repeatedly choose digit 2-(k modulo 4)\nfor an odd k, subtract that digit, then shift k right; this yields terms\n0,+1,-1. Form the positive terms first, then subtract negative terms.\nExamples are 3D=4D-D, 11D=16D-D-4D, 13D=16D+D-4D,\n19D=16D+4D-D, 21D=16D+4D+D, 23D=32D-D-8D,\n25D=32D+D-8D, 27D=32D-D-4D, 29D=32D-D-2D and 31D=32D-D.\nKeep all intermediates 37 bits, so the exact arithmetic is retained.\nDo not explicitly replace the even-product registers with shifts of odd\nregisters: that area-saving probe regressed to 68.083 MHz. Do not use\ncarry-save constant-product logic: that probe regressed to 74.762 MHz.\nPreserve the direct full-bank capture topology and the existing request\nenable. No runtime division, modulo, ROM, vendor primitive or extra cycle.\n\n'''+h[b:]\na=h.index('A temporary radix-32 probe');b=h.index('Adapt internal arithmetic-state assertions',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''A temporary radix-32 probe with this canonical shift/add/subtract bank\npassed lint, the existing pipeline suite, selftest RVFI comparison with\nready and stalled buses, and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/\nmarker validation. CoreMark retained exactly 3978988 timed cycles.\nGowin placements 0/1/2 measured 77.405/78.538/78.538 MHz, using 6598 LUTs,\n2733 registers, zero LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and six DSPs. This implies\n197.382 iterations/s, approximately 3.2 percent higher fitness, below\nacceptance. All three tested radix-32 multiple-bank forms passed the\nadapted real/ALTOPS arithmetic suites; formal has not been run.\n\nPredict three percent higher fitness with low confidence. This is the\nbest measured structural direction in this proposal session, but it has\nnot demonstrated the required tournament margin. The wider bank and\n32-way selection increase routing/fanout, and ordinary EX feedback now\ncompetes with divider launch/recurrence for the critical path. Acceptance\nrequires strictly more than 200.06842 iterations/s, or 79.606984 MHz median\nFmax at unchanged cycles. Measure all three placements and the actual\nmarker-delimited cycles. Preserve nret=1, core ports, every hard invariant\nand all evaluation files. Run unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates;\nALTOPS formal alone does not establish the new real arithmetic.\n\n'''+h[b:]\nd['hypothesis']=h;d['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':3,'confidence':'low'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Replace the launch prefix/radix-16 engine with a 35-bit dividend/quotient,\nzero-remainder initialization and seven radix-32 digits. Capture all\n37-bit divisor multiples 1..31 with canonical signed-digit constant\nshifts/adds/subtracts; use full 38-bit borrow decisions and a balanced\none-hot digit/remainder selection tree. Preserve request/completion\ntiming, sign/exception semantics, snapshots, reset, integer/MUL datapaths\nand the exact ALTOPS branch/controller.'''\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Validated full-bank hypothesis')\nprint('fitness',78.538*1e7/3978988)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
