{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r10s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r10s2',\n'title':\\\"Reuse the fetch predictor's direct-target alignment bit in EX\\\",\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The sixteen-entry agree predictor already captures most direct-control cycle savings. The r7s2 proposal carried two full recovery endpoints into EX and regressed; r8s2 forwarding specialization and r9s2 branch-comparator balancing also regressed. Fetch already determines exact B/J target alignment to qualify prediction, but EX recomputes that classification from its target arithmetic before trap-qualified forwarding, predictor training and recovery. Carry only this one-bit classification with the prediction, preserving the original branch comparator, forwarding equations and target datapaths.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Extend if_id_t and id_ex_t with one direct_misaligned bit adjacent to predicted_taken, keeping valid last and the existing leading operand fields. In IF set it from direct_target[1:0] \"'!= 0 using the same exact B/J immediate and fetch PC already used by the predictor. The flag describes the raw direct target even when the instruction is predicted not-taken. It is not the inverse of predicted_taken. Keep the current prediction policy, sixteen-entry binary agree table, reset state, training schedule and PC[5:2] index unchanged.\n\nCarry this bit through every fixed-head fetch-queue entry and the empty bypass. Capture it in ID/EX under the existing payload enable, with the instruction and saved prediction; retain it across load-use and backend holds. Queue occupancy and instruction validity invalidate stale metadata on redirect/reset. Compute raw metadata independently of readiness and redirect, preserving validity-only squashing.\n\nIn EX replace only the direct-target alignment inputs: misalign_branch = in.ctrl.is_branch && branch_taken && in.direct_misaligned; misalign_jump = in.valid && in.ctrl.is_jump && (in.ctrl.is_jalr ? jalr_sum[1] : in.direct_misaligned). The JALR expression is exact because the ISA clears bit zero before testing four-byte target alignment. Keep its original rs1+immediate adder. Consume the saved direct flag only for decoded conditional branches and JAL, never for JALR or an arbitrary instruction whose raw bits resemble an immediate. Do not assume PC alignment to simplify the precomputed flag: derive it from the actual fetch PC and complete direct target as today.\n\nRetain the existing EX target arithmetic, branch comparator, effective_taken, control_advance, training qualification, saved-direction recovery, ctrl_with_trap, fwd_w_en, jump links and architectural pc_next. A taken misaligned branch or jump must still trap, suppress the link write and recover/fall through according to the existing sequential-trap policy. A not-taken branch with a misaligned encoded target remains nontrapping. Existing training excludes taken misalignment faults and trains other advancing legal branches exactly once. Preserve FENCE.I serialization and all queue, memory, divider and forwarding behavior. No new recovery stage, added branch bubble, full target metadata, predictor capacity change or arithmetic rewrite belongs in this hypothesis.\n\nThis moves one predictor classification across an existing boundary, adding approximately five timed metadata flops for the four-entry queue plus ID/EX instead of the wide endpoint replication attempted in r7s2. It aims to remove target-adder/alignment fanout from the EX predictor/trap path while leaving branch outcome and architectural timing unchanged. Predict five percent higher fitness with low confidence. The comparison, divider launch and multiply-feedback paths may still dominate, and changed placement can overwhelm the local improvement. No measured fitness improvement is claimed.\n\nRequire directed checks for both values of the flag independently of prediction direction, B/J positive and negative immediates with bit one set/clear, taken and not-taken branches, all branch conditions, legal/misaligned JAL, and every JALR low-bit sum with bit-zero clearing. Preserve all existing predictor, FIFO-conservation, stall, forwarding, trap, RVFI-order and progress assertions. Adapt packed-bundle extraction to the new metadata bit without deleting architectural or cycle assertions. Test queue bypass, full queues, simultaneous push/pop, same-index training, reset and redirect, unavailable imem and prolonged dmem/divider holds; wrong-path stores must remain impossible.\n\nRun unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates plus canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker validation under both bus-stall streams. Expect exactly 3978988 timed CoreMark cycles because prediction and pipeline cadence are unchanged. Score all three Gowin placements. Acceptance above 191.27 * 1.046 = 200.06842 iterations/second needs approximately 79.607 MHz median Fmax at this cycle count. Preserve nret=1, all top-level ports, default-illegal decoding, real/ALTOPS M semantics, every hard invariant and all evaluation files.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add one direct_misaligned metadata bit to if_id_t and id_ex_t adjacent to predicted_taken. Preserve leading operand fields, valid-last convention, downstream bundles and the nret=1 external interface.'},\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Emit direct_target[1:0] \"'!= 0 as raw_fetch.direct_misaligned independently of readiness, recovery and predicted direction. Carry it automatically through the packed queue entries and empty bypass. Preserve all prediction, counter-training, queue and PC-update behavior.'\"'},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Capture and retain the alignment bit alongside predicted_taken with the unchanged payload enable and hold behavior. Keep fully forwarded operand capture and validity-only recovery unchanged.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use the captured flag for conditional-branch and direct-JAL target alignment, and jalr_sum[1] for JALR alignment after bit-zero clearing. Preserve all downstream trap, forwarding, training, recovery and architectural-successor equations and the original branch comparator and target arithmetic.'},\n{'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'Update packed-bundle reference construction for the extra alignment bit. Preserve FIFO conservation, prediction and counter assertions; check independent alignment metadata association through bypass, all occupancies, simultaneous push/pop, alias updates, stalls, redirects and reset.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Update packed-bundle extraction without relaxing architectural or timing assertions. Add focused B/J alignment-metadata and JALR low-bit cases, including not-taken misaligned branches, taken traps, suppressed link writes, mixed control transfers, held entries, recovery and wrong-path stores.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Replaced and schema-validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
