{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"agent_message","text":"The baseline reproduced its recorded timing; the alignment probe also regressed. I’m finalizing a different, unmeasured hypothesis: decode branch comparison type into one-hot controls in ID, then register them for EX. This moves selection decoding earlier while preserving the existing comparators and prediction policy. Confidence is low."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r10s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r10s2',\n'title':'Predecode branch comparison classes before the predictor resolution stage',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The current sixteen-entry agree predictor already captures most direct-control cycle savings. Previous r8s2 forwarding specialization and r9s2 comparator balancing regressed. Both retained a binary branch_op field decoded again in EX, where selection, branch outcome, predictor recovery and trap-qualified forwarding form a feedback path to ID. Move only the branch-condition selection decode before ID/EX, using registered one-hot comparison classes while retaining the original word-wide comparison operators and predictor policy.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add a three-bit branch_class and a branch_invert bit to ctrl_t, captured with the existing decoded controls in ID/EX. Decode dec_branch_op in ID as follows: BEQ/BNE select class 001 (equality), BLT/BGE select 010 (signed less-than), BLTU/BGEU select 100 (unsigned less-than). Set branch_invert for BNE, BGE and BGEU. For reserved comparison encodings select 000 and clear branch_invert. Derive these controls from the validated decoder outputs, independent of readiness, redirect, producer selection and branch outcome. Preserve decoder default-illegal behavior. Existing branch_op may remain for interface/test compatibility; synthesis may prune its unused registered copy.\n\nIn EX retain three ordinary word-wide comparison expressions: eq=(rs1==rs2), slt=(\"'$signed(rs1)<$signed(rs2)), and ult=(rs1<rs2), using the current fully forwarded, registered source operands. Replace only the six-way binary branch_op case selection with branch_cond=((in.ctrl.branch_class[0] && eq) || (in.ctrl.branch_class[1] && slt) || (in.ctrl.branch_class[2] && ult)) ''^ in.ctrl.branch_invert. The registered classes are one-hot or zero. With zero class the inversion bit must be zero. Equality for BGE/BGEU is handled by inversion of strict less-than. Do not introduce a nibble/byte comparison tree, an operand-sign bias network, speculative history, or an additional pipeline stage.\n\nThe architectural change is moving instruction-class selection across the existing ID/EX boundary. The late EX outcome path sees registered selection bits and a masked-OR plus polarity operation rather than decoding funct3 to choose among six conditions. This adds at most four control bits to the RTL bundle; the now-unused three-bit branch_op register can disappear from the timed netlist. It does not move operand comparison into ID or lengthen its forwarding datapath with arithmetic. Gowin may already perform equivalent logic factoring, so timing improvement is uncertain.\n\nKeep every downstream branch equation unchanged: branch_taken, branch/jump target adders, alignment faults, ctrl_with_trap, fwd_w_en, effective_taken, redirect_target, train_valid/train_index/train_agree and EX/MEM.pc_next. Preserve the sixteen-entry binary agree table, PC[5:2] index, reset and simultaneous read/write semantics, early JAL, sequential JALR, fixed-head four-entry queue and captured predicted_taken metadata. Correct predictions retain zero recovery bubbles; held branches train and recover only when EX advances. Retain validity-only squashing, recovery priority over unavailable imem, FENCE.I serialization, all memory and divider handshakes, jump links, sequential trap fallback and retirement order. No counter recoding, capacity change, forwarding-predicate specialization or delayed recovery belongs in this hypothesis.\n\nPredict five percent higher fitness with low confidence. This specific registered-predecode topology has not been measured. An unmodified placement-0 check reproduced 73.244 MHz. Exploratory alternatives in this session failed to beat it: thermometer counters 62.069 MHz, four/eight-entry tables 66.897/64.440 MHz, delayed conditional recovery 67.786 MHz, combinational factored/sign-biased selection 61.479/59.166 MHz, and carrying a target-alignment bit 55.669 MHz. These results argue against claiming a demonstrated gain. The proposed predecode differs from the combinational selection probes by registering the comparison-class decode in ID and preserving separate ordinary signed/unsigned comparators. Unrelated divider-launch and EX-result paths may still dominate.\n\nVerify the class mapping and resulting predicate against the original six-way case for all 32-bit operand pairs and all eight branch_op values with a combinational equivalence check. Retain every existing decoder, predictor, FIFO-conservation, pipeline, forwarding, trap, RVFI and progress assertion. Exercise equality, opposite signs, signed extrema, unsigned wrap boundaries, all legal branch functions, reserved encodings, taken/not-taken and aligned/misaligned targets. Verify class and polarity stay associated with the instruction across queue delivery, load-use bubbles, unavailable imem, dmem holds, divider completion, redirects and reset; no wrong-path memory effect is allowed.\n\nRun unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks under both bus-stall streams. Policy and cadence are unchanged, so expect exactly 3978988 timed CoreMark cycles. Score all three Gowin placements. Acceptance above 191.27 * 1.046 = 200.06842 iterations/second requires approximately 79.607 MHz median Fmax at that cycle count. Preserve nret=1, all top-level ports, default-illegal decoding, real/ALTOPS M semantics, every hard invariant and all evaluation files.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add three-bit branch_class and one-bit branch_invert controls to ctrl_t. Preserve existing leading operand fields, instr