{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"None of the timing probes beat the champion. I’m submitting one unmeasured predictor hypothesis: fold the saved prediction into an ID-stage recovery mask, so EX can detect a wrong prediction directly from the comparator result. The file will state low confidence and make no claim of a measured gain."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r11s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r11s2',\n 'title':'Predecode the predicted branch outcome into a registered recovery mask',\n 'category':'predictor',\n 'motivation':'''The champion already predicts direct branches and JAL. Recent r9s2 and\nr10s2 comparator balancing and comparison-class predecode changed no\nCoreMark cycles and lost Fmax. The remaining predictor opportunity is\nthe late recovery dependency: the current EX path selects an architectural\nbranch condition, qualifies taken/alignment, then compares against the\nsaved predicted_taken bit. Prediction is already known in ID, so its\npolarity can be folded into registered recovery controls before EX.\n\nA retirement-order profile of the canonical timed region found 2922016\ninstructions, 529588 conditional branches and only 13735 JALRs. Its\nsixteen-entry agree model missed 55124 directions. These are software\nprofile counts, not cycle-accurate predictor measurements. They argue\nagainst expecting the acceptance margin from a JALR target table alone.\nThe proposed change targets recovery timing with unchanged prediction\npolicy and pipeline cadence.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Add a six-bit branch_recover_mask to id_ex_t. This mask describes which\nprimitive comparison outcome would contradict the prediction already\nattached to the selected IF/ID instruction. Generate it in ID from the\nvalidated branch control, branch_op and in.predicted_taken, independently\nof operand values. Keep the existing encoded branch_op and architectural\nbranch comparator. This is one predictor-resolution retiming: move the\ncombination of instruction condition and prediction polarity before the\nID/EX register, rather than merely registering comparison classes.\n\nDefine mask bits [0..5] as recovery on EQ, NE, signed-LT, signed-GE,\nunsigned-LT, unsigned-GE respectively. For a legal conditional branch\npredicted not taken, set its natural condition bit: BEQ->0, BNE->1,\nBLT->2, BGE->3, BLTU->4, BGEU->5. For the same branch predicted taken,\nset the opposite bit within its pair (natural index XOR 1). All other\ninstructions and reserved branch encodings get mask zero. Exactly one\nbit is set for a legal branch. Capture under the existing ID/EX payload\nenable, reset to zero, and retain across backend_hold and load_use.\nPrediction must come from the selected queue entry, not from the raw\nfetch address or the current predictor table. Keep leading PC/operand\nfields and trailing instr/predicted_taken/valid placement consistent with\ntest helpers, inserting the new field before ctrl or instr.\n\nIn EX compute the ordinary full-width primitive results eq=(rs1==rs2),\nslt=(\"'$signed(rs1)<$signed(rs2)), and ult=(rs1<rs2), using the current\nregistered, fully forwarded operands. Produce raw_branch_mismatch as\n(mask[0]&eq) | (mask[1]&!eq) | (mask[2]&slt) |\n(mask[3]&!slt) | (mask[4]&ult) | (mask[5]&!ult).\nUse a balanced OR of the three two-term condition pairs, not a priority\nselection. The registered mask includes prediction polarity, so this\npath does not select branch_cond and subsequently XOR predicted_taken.\nDo not add syn_keep or duplicate operand registers. The existing\narchitectural branch_cond case may share these primitive results, but\nits behavior, signedness and reserved-selector default remain unchanged.\n\nHandle alignment separately and exactly. Let direct_aligned be\n(branch_target[1:0]==0). Define branch_mismatch = direct_aligned ?\nraw_branch_mismatch : in.predicted_taken. An unaligned direct target\ncan never be an effective taken successor under the existing trap\npolicy, so comparison against the saved direction reduces to that bit.\nUse control_advance && in.ctrl.is_branch && branch_mismatch for branch\nrecovery. Keep the original effective_taken-versus-predicted_taken test\nfor JAL/JALR and the original unconditional fence_i_advance term. The\nsame control_advance qualification must prevent updates or recovery from\ninvalid, illegal, reset or held EX instructions.\n\nKeep branch_taken, misalign_branch, misalign_jump, ctrl_with_trap,\nfwd_w_en, branch/jump target adders, redirect_target, train_valid,\ntrain_index, train_agree and EX/MEM.pc_next behavior unchanged. In\nparticular do not use the recovery mask as architectural branch_taken,\nchange a misalignment trap, suppress its required link-write blocking,\nor repeat the earlier forwarding-eligibility specialization. Saved\ndirection still selects the direct correction endpoint exactly as today.\nEX/MEM.pc_next and RVFI must always describe the resolved successor.\n\nPreserve the sixteen-entry binary agree table, PC[5:2] indexing, weakly\nagree reset, pre-edge read/write semantics, early JAL, sequential JALR,\nfour-entry fixed-head elastic queue and empty bypass. Preserve recovery\npriority over unavailable imem, full queue flushing, FENCE.I ordering,\nvalidity-only squashing, payload independence from redirect, all memory\nand divide handshakes, arithmetic, decoder legality, nret=1, all external\nports and every hard invariant. No new pipeline stage or recovery bubble\nis introduced; expect the champion'\"'s 3978988 timed CoreMark cycles.\n\nPredict five percent higher fitness with low confidence. This exact\nprediction-conditioned mask has not been implemented or timed. It is\nnot the r10s2 comparison-class predecode: that variant left prediction\npolarity after the selected architectural condition. Exploratory probes\nin this session rejected one-hot counters (66.947 MHz in placement 0)\nand cached one-hot prediction (62.266 MHz). Moving comparison slices\ninto ID also failed: the best full-slice probe, eight four-bit groups,\nreached 72.338 MHz median with unchanged cycles and valid CoreMark CRCs;\nasymmetric low-part retiming reached only 56.099-66.815 MHz in placement\n0. None is part of this proposal. They show why operand retiming and\ncounter recoding should not be bundled into this attempt. The proposed\nmask changes only instruction/prediction control preparation in ID.\n\nThe risk is that Gowin already folds these Boolean operations, or that\nunchanged branch-to-forwarding, divider launch and ALU-to-ID paths dominate.\nAdded mask registers and fanout can also lower Fmax. Require unchanged\nformal, full small-program RVFI cosimulation with both stall modes,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and all three vendor\nplacements. Acceptance above 191.27*1.046=200.06842 iterations/second\nrequires approximately 79.607 MHz median at the expected cycle count.\nDo not claim improvement from predicate equivalence or a single placement.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add a six-bit branch_recover_mask to id_ex_t only. Preserve existing architectural controls, full registered operands, saved prediction, bundle association and nret=1 interfaces.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Map validated branch_op and the selected instruction\\\\'s predicted_taken to a one-hot primitive-outcome recovery mask. Capture with existing payload enable; clear on reset and retain on holds. Do not compare operands in ID or read current predictor state to reconstruct a queued prediction.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Compute prediction disagreement directly from the registered mask and ordinary equality/signed-less/unsigned-less results. Qualify conditional recovery with the exact alignment fallback and unchanged control_advance. Preserve architectural branch resolution, traps, forwarding, direct correction data, training, jump recovery, FENCE.I and downstream RVFI successors.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain all existing predictor/FIFO/architectural assertions. Check all six legal branch functions, both saved prediction directions, reserved/nonbranch zero masks and hold stability. Prove the new branch recovery predicate equals ((actual_taken && aligned) \"'!= predicted_taken) for arbitrary operands, predictions and alignment; test equal/opposite-sign/extreme operands. Exercise queued predictions changed by subsequent training, load-use bubbles, long dmem/divider holds, imem stalls, misaligned targets, reset, FENCE.I and wrong-path stores. Preserve exact retirement order, links, traps, operands and expected cycle schedule; adjust only packed-layout helpers if needed.'\"'}\n ]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\nprint('Wrote schema-valid final hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
