tured pc_plus4.\nKeep the architectural JALR rs1+immediate calculation and all ordinary\ninteger, multiply, divider, forwarding, and register-file logic intact.\n\nSeparate direction recovery from target data: a saved taken prediction\nselects the registered sequential endpoint for correction; a saved\nnot-taken prediction selects the registered direct endpoint or the\nexisting JALR result. Resolve against the saved predicted_taken bit,\nexactly as today, since direct targets remain exact and aligned and\nJALR stays unpredicted. Compute actual EX/MEM.pc_next independently of\nprediction, including PC+4 fallback and suppressed link writ\n…[18958 of 22030 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e5dcd3fab9a36dc7]…\n comparison slices\ninto ID also failed: the best full-slice probe, eight four-bit groups,\nreached 72.338 MHz median with unchanged cycles and valid CoreMark CRCs;\nasymmetric low-part retiming reached only 56.099-66.815 MHz in placement\n0. None is part of this proposal. They show why operand retiming and\ncounter recoding should not be bundled into this attempt. The proposed\nmask changes only instruction/prediction control preparation in ID.\n\nThe risk is that Gowin already folds these Boolean operations, or that\nunchanged branch-to-forwarding, divider launch and ALU-to-ID paths dominate.\nAdded mask registers and fanout can also lower Fmax. Require unchanged\nformal, full small-program RVFI cosimulation with both stall modes,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks and all three vendor\nplacements. Acceptance above 191.27*1.046=200.06842 iterations/second\nrequires approximately 79.607 MHz median at the expected cycle count.\nDo not claim improvement from predicate equivalence or a single placement.\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
