e the branch comparator and all six legal\nbranch conditions. The raw direct target, including its low alignment\nbits, must be retained even when fetch declines to predict it taken.\n\nCapture endpoints using the unchanged ID/EX payload enable, together\nwith that instruction's PC and prediction. Hold them throughout backend\nstalls and load-use holds. Recovery may affect only PC selection and\nID/EX validity; it must not enter payload enables, raw instruction data,\nregister-file read addresses, load-use comparison, or forwarding data.\nPreserve valid as the final bundle field and the leading registered\noperand fields. Invalid entries have no architectural side effects.\n\nPreserve the curren\n…[12744 of 15816 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a9a130b38e3c0300]…\nin every existing decoder, predictor, FIFO-conservation, pipeline, forwarding, trap, RVFI and progress assertion. Exercise equality, opposite signs, signed extrema, unsigned wrap boundaries, all legal branch functions, reserved encodings, taken/not-taken and aligned/misaligned targets. Verify class and polarity stay associated with the instruction across queue delivery, load-use bubbles, unavailable imem, dmem holds, divider completion, redirects and reset; no wrong-path memory effect is allowed.\n\nRun unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks under both bus-stall streams. Policy and cadence are unchanged, so expect exactly 3978988 timed CoreMark cycles. Score all three Gowin placements. Acceptance above 191.27 * 1.046 = 200.06842 iterations/second requires approximately 79.607 MHz median Fmax at that cycle count. Preserve nret=1, all top-level ports, default-illegal decoding, real/ALTOPS M semantics, every hard invariant and all evaluation files.\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
