{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r13s2.yaml; cat cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md; sed -n '90,155p' Makefile; sed -n '1,150p' tools/eval/gowin.py\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Resolve predictor outcomes with a carry-free two-bit comparison tree\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion already has direct prediction and a four-entry fetch queue.\n  Its reported worst path starts at ID/EX.rs2_val and ends at the fetch PC,\n  crossing branch resolution and recovery. More prediction capacity offers\n  little cycle headroom: an architectural profile of the canonical timed\n  region contains 529588 conditional branches but only 13735 JALRs, and\n  prior profiling reported 55124 direction misses. Repeated control-mask\n  and counter-update predecodes in r10s2-r12s2 failed to clear acceptance.\n  The earlier r9s2 nibble comparator also regressed; this proposal tests\n  a different, explicitly Boolean LUT4 comparator on the new champion,\n  where the recorded recovery path is now the bottleneck.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the operand-comparison network used for branch prediction\n  resolution in EX with a balanced tree of sixteen two-bit comparisons.\n  Build each leaf from Boolean expressions, not a behavioral less-than\n  operator or subtractor. For bits h=2*i+1 and l=2*i, define\n  E_i = !(rs1[h]^rs2[h]) && !(rs1[l]^rs2[l]) and\n  L_i = (!rs1[h] && rs2[h]) ||\n        (!(rs1[h]^rs2[h]) && !rs1[l] && rs2[l]).\n  Each leaf function has four primary inputs and fits a LUT4. Merge\n  adjacent high/low groups as E=E_high && E_low and\n  L=L_high || (E_high && L_low), in four balanced levels. Higher bits\n  always take priority. The resulting E is word equality and L is\n  unsigned less-than. Signed less-than equals rs1[31] when sign bits\n  differ, otherwise L. Keep the original six-way branch_op case and\n  reserved-selector false default, substituting these three predicates\n  for the current full-width comparisons. Complements implement BNE,\n  BGE and BGEU. Do not change scalar ALU SLT/SLTU comparisons.\n\n  This is a predictor-resolution timing hypothesis, not a prediction\n  policy change. The intended mechanism is to replace a possible\n  word-wide carry path with four-inpu\n…[10529 of 13601 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ca1e82a64510d104]…\n\n    }\n\n\ndef _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Run the build; True if it hit BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC (its process group is\n    killed).\"\"\"\n    import subprocess\n    with log.open(\"w\") as f:\n        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n                                stdout=f, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n                                env=env, start_new_session=True)\n        try:\n            proc.wait(timeout=BUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC)\n            return False\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n            try:\n                os.killpg(proc.pid, 9)\n            except ProcessLookupError:\n                pass\n            proc.wait()\n            return True\n\n\ndef build(worktree: str | Path, rtl_dir: str | Path, bench_sv: str,\n                place_option: int, outdir: str | Path, env: dict | None = None) -> dict:\n    worktree, rtl_dir, outdir = Path(worktree).resolve(), Path(rtl_dir).resolve(), Path(outdir).resolve()\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
