{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_52", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r14s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r14s2',\n'title':'Flatten predictor recovery into a parallel three-source fetch-PC update',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion's reproduced worst placement-0 path starts at a registered branch operand and ends at the fetch PC clock-enable pin. The late redirect drives a high-fanout enable as well as PC selection. Earlier banked PCs left redirect on a recovery-bank enable and added an active-PC mux. Keep one PC register and express its three sources in a parallel data-selection network.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the current predictor and single fetch PC, but replace the priority-coded PC write/hold structure with a full-width, parallel masked-OR update. Keep next_pc = predicted_taken ? direct_target : pc+4 unchanged. Define pc_input = ({32{redirect}} & redirect_target) | ({32{\"'!redirect && fetch_accept}} & next_pc) | ({32{!redirect && !fetch_accept}} & pc). On every non-reset edge assign pc <= pc_input; reset still selects RESET_PC. The masks are mutually exclusive and exhaustive, so this is exactly the existing PC recurrence for every combination of redirect, readiness and queue occupancy, including arbitrary full-width correction addresses.\n\nThe intended timing mechanism is to place recovery, predicted advance and hold in one parallel selection network instead of expressing late redirect as both a priority mux control and an explicit wide register enable. Inspect the vendor netlist and timing: source syntax alone cannot guarantee that synthesis removes clock enables. This proposal has no extra PC bank, active-address mux, pipeline stage, prediction state or recovery cycle. Do not replace the direct/sequential successor mux with a four-source flat selector or put a zero-displacement hold ahead of a shared adder; measured probes of those alternatives were weaker.\n\nKeep all sixteen binary agree counters, indexing, reset, current-state saturating updates and pre-edge lookup semantics. Preserve direct branch/JAL prediction, sequential JALR, exact saved predicted_taken association, four fixed-head queue entries, empty bypass, occupancy transitions and raw fetch data. Recovery still overrides unavailable imem or a full queue, flushes younger entries and is issued only on EX advancement. FENCE.I serialization, held-branch training, misalignment traps, architectural RVFI successors and link writes retain their current behavior. Change only if_stage PC input logic; leave the EX comparator, redirect equations, forwarding, memory requests, ALU and divider intact. Preserve nret=1, all external ports, decoder legality, every hard invariant and all evaluation files.\n\nAn exact exploratory implementation measured 84.451/89.848/89.848 MHz across Gowin options 0/1/2, with 6567 LUTs, 2801 registers, zero LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. At the expected unchanged 3984075 marker-delimited cycles, this corresponds to roughly 225.515 iterations/s, only 0.30 percent above the champion. It is the strongest isolated predictor probe in this session but does not demonstrate the required 4.6 percent acceptance margin; the integer expected gain is rounded to zero with low confidence. Unchanged ALU-to-ID and divider paths constrain further improvement. Do not claim this result as an accepted improvement.\n\nProve the full-width PC recurrence equivalent over arbitrary reset, redirect, target, fetch_accept, prediction and PC values. Keep all existing fetch-queue conservation and pipeline assertions; exercise recovery during imem stalls, full/empty queues, simultaneous training, adjacent redirects, reset and wrong-path stores. Require unchanged full formal and RVFI cosimulation gates, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks under both stall streams and all three vendor placements. Full-core formal and RVFI cosimulation remain implementation gates, not completed claims. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 235.17218 iterations/s, about 93.695 MHz at unchanged cycles.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':0,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Preserve the existing predictor, next_pc calculation, FIFO and all interfaces. Add the full-width three-source pc_input masked-OR expression and capture it every non-reset edge. Keep reset priority and prove exact equivalence to reset/redirect/fetch_accept/hold PC semantics. Inspect mapped PC data and enable paths rather than assuming a particular inference.'},\n {'file':'test/test_if_stage.py','description':'Retain all conservation and predictor assertions. Add full-width PC recurrence checks across arbitrary redirects, wraparound, backpressure, full queue holds, reset and concurrent table training; compare against the original priority recurrence.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Retain every architectural, progress and cycle assertion. Exercise correct and incorrect predictions, held control transfers, unavailable imem during recovery, FENCE.I, JALR and misalignment. Check retirement PCs, successors, order, links and suppression of wrong-path memory effects.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=92))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
