ogether with\\ncombinational B/J immediate extraction and a shared PC-relative target\\nadder. Reset counters to weakly taken (2'b10). Predict legal conditional\\nbranches from the counter MSB and legal JAL instructions unconditionally\\ntaken; predict all other instructions, including JALR, sequentially.\\nOnly predict an aligned \n…[363105 of 366177 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9f6781aeb9d2833c]…\na_pct\": 0.31, \"vs_baseline\": 1760.73, \"fmax_mhz\": 89.848, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3984075, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6567, \"ff\": 2801, \"seeds\": [84.451, 89.848, 89.848], \"perturbations\": [[0, 84.451, 10], [1, 89.848, 10], [2, 89.848, 10]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_8_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_27_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.841, \"arrival_ns\": 17.136, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T15:55:19.137212Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r14s2 (regression, +0.31%): Flattening single-PC recovery/advance/hold into a parallel masked-OR mux yields only 0.31% at unchanged CoreMark cycles with ALU-to-ID and divider paths still constraining timing, so local recovery-mux restructuring alone misses the 4.6% acceptance margin.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
