{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_34", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'syn_ramstyle|distributed_ram|RAM16|SSRAM' cores tools docs | head -60; ls /opt/gowin/IDE/doc | head\"", "aggregated_output": "rg: docs: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv:32:  (* syn_ramstyle = \"registers\" *) logic [31:0] regs [0:31];\ntools/eval/gowin.py:121:        \"lutram\": _cells(r, \"--SSRAM(RAM16)\") or 0,\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:8:- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r4s1 (improvement, +8.78%): Capturing fully forwarded operands in ID/EX and forcing flop register-file storage with `syn_ramstyle = \"registers\"` removes late forwarding from EX arithmetic paths, improving timing without extra CoreMark cycles at increased LUT/flip-flop cost.\ntools/eval/test_fpga_report.py:20:    --SSRAM(RAM16)            | 8                                   | -\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Resolve forwarding before the ID/EX operand registers\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 116.47 at 52.313 MHz median Fmax and 4491485\\nmarker-delimited CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md and the structural entries\\nin log.jsonl show that divider isolation and validity-only squashing\\nremoved earlier timing bottlenecks. A fresh make timing TARGET=bench\\nreproduced its placement-option-0 result of 48.369 MHz. The detailed\\n25.969 ns path starts at register-file BSRAM output, passes through ID\\ndata selection, several EX forwarding/operand muxes, the signed DSP\\nmultiplier, and result selection before reaching the data-memory input.\\nThe multiplier is only part of this path; operand selection precedes\\nevery execute operation, including divider normalization and launch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion scores 116.47 at 52.313 MHz median Fmax and 4491485\\nmarker-delimited CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md and the structural entries\\nin log.jsonl show that divider isolation and validity-only squashing\\nremoved earlier timing bottlenecks. A fresh make timing TARGET=bench\\nreproduced its placement-option-0 result of 48.369 MHz. The detailed\\n25.969 ns path starts at register-file BSRAM output, passes through ID\\ndata selection, several EX forwarding/operand muxes, the signe\n…[40278 of 43350 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4869a34c9fea59b7]…\n \"perturbations\": [[0, 65.508, 17], [1, 67.751, 9], [2, 67.751, 9]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.is_auipc_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/remainder_q_3_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -10.265, \"arrival_ns\": 20.56, \"logic_cells\": 19, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 17, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T08:48:53.445235Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r6s2 (improvement, +5.62%): A 16-entry agree predictor plus early JAL complements the parallel radix-16 divider by removing direct-control-flow bubbles while preserving fully forwarded ID/EX operands and validity-only recovery, raising CoreMark throughput from 152.61 to 161.18 iterations/s.\"}\nCN\nEN\nJP\nRN100-1.9.11.03EducationE_Gowin Software Education Version Release Note.pdf\nRN100-1.9.11.03EducationJ_Gowinソフトウェア(教育版)リリースノート.pdf\nRN100-1.9.11.03Education_Gowin云源软件教育版本发布说明.pdf\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
