{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());d['title']='Register agree-predictor training feedback without delaying recovery'\nd['motivation']='''The successful sixteen-entry agree predictor already captures nearly all\nof the cycle benefit measured for the larger BHT: 4203513 versus 4201709\nCoreMark cycles. Its EX-resolved outcome drives counter update logic as\nwell as branch recovery and misalignment handling. The champion's full\nGowin path includes branch-comparison carry cells, cells named train_next,\nand trap-adjusted forwarding eligibility before returning to ID/EX operands.\nThese names reflect synthesis sharing, not a literal RTL feedback path\nthrough the predictor. This motivates isolating predictor training fanout\nbehind a small register while preserving the successful lookup circuit.\n\nProbes during hypothesis generation found that additional recovery state,\ndistributed counter updates, static prediction and one-bit counters all\nlost first-placement Fmax. Retaining the centralized two-bit table and\nregistering only its training event is the narrower remaining experiment.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Keep the sixteen-entry two-bit agree predictor exactly as implemented,\nincluding its centralized saturating counter update, backward/forward\nbias, aligned direct-target generation, early JAL and saved-direction\nrecovery. Add a one-cycle registered training record between EX resolution\nand the existing table updater. The record contains valid, four-bit index\nand agree outcome. It accepts one resolution per cycle and is consumed\nunconditionally at the following edge; consecutive branches cannot\noverflow it. Reset clears record validity and its payload. Preserve the\nexisting counter reset to weak agreement (10). Capture index and agree\nevery cycle rather than gating their capture with late train_valid.\n\nThe existing EX train_valid remains qualified by valid legal conditional\nbranch advancement, \"'!reset, !stall_ex_mem and no target-alignment fault.\nA held branch enqueues nothing until it advances. A bubble clears the next\nrecord'\"'s valid bit while the previous valid record can update the table.\nRecovery must not discard an already-resolved older branch's queued update;\na squashed younger branch must never enqueue. Do not add stalls or a\nbackpressure path for predictor training, and do not register recovery.\n\nFeed the existing train_counter/train_next combinational logic and indexed\nbitplane writes from the REGISTERED index, outcome and valid. Keep the\ncurrent saturating arithmetic and bitplane organization unchanged. Update\nthe counter's current value, never a value saved at fetch or resolution,\nso back-to-back same-index updates accumulate correctly at saturation too.\nFetch continues to read pre-edge state and saves the exact prediction used\nwith the instruction. Add no same-cycle bypass from incoming or queued\ntraining. The extra training latency can change an adjacent aliased branch's\nprediction, but existing EX resolution remains the correctness authority.\n\nMake no changes to branch/jump target arithmetic, redirect qualification,\nID payload enables, validity-only squash, forwarding, multiplier, divider,\npipeline depth, interface ports or architectural/RVFI reporting. This is\none predictor-training retiming hypothesis. Its intended timing benefit is\nseparating branch-outcome fanout from counter-read/update/decode logic;\nit does not claim improved branch accuracy or fewer recovery bubbles.\n\nAn isolated RTL probe of this exact centralized queued-training design\ncompleted stalled CoreMark in 4203504 marker-delimited cycles versus\n4203513 for the champion, with all canonical CRCs, validation UART literal,\nnormal EBREAK and no out-of-bounds access. This nine-cycle difference is\nnegligible; a gain must come from Fmax. Formal and the delayed-training\nscoreboard have not yet been run for this probe. Preserve their full checks.\n\nPredict six percent higher fitness with low confidence, subject to vendor\nmeasurement. Extra registers and placement changes can lose timing, and\nthe unchanged divider recurrence is already nearly as slow as the worst\npath. At 4203504 cycles, acceptance above 181.38 * 1.046 = 189.72348\niterations/second requires median Fmax above about 79.751 MHz. Require all\nthree Gowin placements and greater than 4.6 percent measured fitness\nimprovement; a single placement is not sufficient evidence of acceptance.\n\nPreserve nret=1, all decoder/trap invariants, memory bounds/handshakes,\nexact-once architectural effects, the ten-cycle branch-to-divide progress\nbound and real/ALTOPS M arithmetic. Run unchanged formal, adapted full\npredictor/pipeline tests, cosimulation and canonical CRC/UART validation.\nDo not alter any evaluation contract or weaken any existing assertion.\n'''\nd['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Add resettable training valid/index/agree registers without\nbackpressure. Capture incoming EX feedback every cycle and use the\nprevious record to drive the existing centralized train_counter,\ntrain_next and indexed bitplane writes. Preserve table capacity,\ncounter arithmetic, lookup, pre-edge read/write behavior, bias,\ntarget generation, fetch acceptance and recovery priority.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Model the additional training cycle in the predictor scoreboard,\ndistinguishing EX enqueue from table application while retaining all\narchitectural, saved-prediction and recovery assertions. Check every\ncounter state/outcome, consecutive same-index and different-index\nbranches, saturation, a queued update during a later backend hold,\nimem unavailability, redirect, bubbles and reset. Assert no stale\ncounter overwrite, lost update, repeated held-branch training or\nwrong-path enqueue. Keep branch-to-divide progress checks unchanged.\n'''}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda dumper,s:dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=85));jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined to centralized queued training and validated schema')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_53", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());d['title']='Register agree-predictor training feedback without delaying recovery'\nd['motivation']='''The successful sixteen-entry agree predictor already captures nearly all\nof the cycle benefit measured for the larger BHT: 4203513 versus 4201709\nCoreMark cycles. Its EX-resolved outcome drives counter update logic as\nwell as branch recovery and misalignment handling. The champion's full\nGowin path includes branch-comparison carry cells, cells named train_next,\nand trap-adjusted forwarding eligibility before returning to ID/EX operands.\nThese names reflect synthesis sharing, not a literal RTL feedback path\nthrough the predictor. This motivates isolating predictor training fanout\nbehind a small register while preserving the successful lookup circuit.\n\nProbes during hypothesis generation found that additional recovery state,\ndistributed counter updates, static prediction and one-bit counters all\nlost first-placement Fmax. Retaining the centralized two-bit table and\nregistering only its training event is the narrower remaining experiment.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Keep the sixteen-entry two-bit agree predictor exactly as implemented,\nincluding its centralized saturating counter update, backward/forward\nbias, aligned direct-target generation, early JAL and saved-direction\nrecovery. Add a one-cycle registered training record between EX resolution\nand the existing table updater. The record contains valid, four-bit index\nand agree outcome. It accepts one resolution per cycle and is consumed\nunconditionally at the following edge; consecutive branches cannot\noverflow it. Reset clears record validity and its payload. Preserve the\nexisting counter reset to weak agreement (10).