{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"ls -la /srv/hwebench/tmp/84625fbe/367e0996 && rg --files -uuu cores/bench | head -80 && sed -n '1,130p' test/cosim/reference.py\"", "aggregated_output": "total 24\ndrwxrwx---+ 6 nobody   nogroup  4096 Oct  2 13:03 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody   nogroup  4096 Oct  2 13:01 ..\ndr-xr-xr-x  2 hwebench hwebench   40 Oct  2 13:03 .agents\ndr-xr-xr-x  2 hwebench hwebench   40 Oct  2 13:03 .codex\ndr-xr-xr-x  2 hwebench hwebench   40 Oct  2 13:03 .git\ndrwxrwx---+ 9 hwebench hwebench 4096 Oct  2 13:03 codex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1001\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_if_stage.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu_altops.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\ncores/bench/core.yaml\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\ncores/bench/experiments/.gitkeep\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"RV32IM reference interpreter for the cosim. Mirrors the DUT's trap\ndiscipline so cosim traces stay aligned across illegal / misaligned\nencodings.\n\nTrap policy (matches rtl/decoder.sv default-illegal + rtl/ex_stage.sv +\nrtl/mem_stage.sv misalign traps):\n\n  - Reserved R-type:        funct7=0x20 with fn3 ∈ {1,2,3,4,6,7}\n  - Reserved OP-IMM shifts: SLLI/SRLI/SRAI with disallowed funct7\n  - Reserved LOAD funct3:   3, 6, 7\n  - Reserved STORE funct3:  3..7\n  - Reserved BRANCH funct3: 2, 3\n  - JALR funct3 != 0\n  - Non-EBREAK SYSTEM:      ECALL, CSR ops, MRET, …\n  - Unknown opcode (AMO etc.)\n  - Misaligned LH/LHU/LW/SH/SW\n  - Misaligned BRANCH (taken) / JAL / JALR target\n\nOn trap the retirement is reported with rvfi_trap=1, rd_addr=0,\nrd_wdata=0, mem_*\n…[3549 of 6621 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d4f9f6f9e5137304]…\nurn -r if a < 0 else r\n\n    def _retire(self, *, pc, npc, instr, trap=0,\n                wrd=0, wval=0, rs1=0, rs2=0,\n                rs1_rdata_pre=0, rs2_rdata_pre=0,\n                mem_addr=0, mem_rmask=0, mem_rdata=0,\n                mem_wmask=0, mem_wdata=0):\n        \"\"\"Centralized retirement record. On trap=1 we zero out the\n        write-side fields and force npc = pc + 4 so the trace stays in\n        lockstep with the DUT (which suppresses redirects + reg/mem\n        commits on misalign / illegal).\"\"\"\n        if trap:\n            wrd = wval = 0\n            mem_addr = mem_rmask = mem_wmask = 0\n            mem_rdata = mem_wdata = 0\n            npc = (pc + 4) & MASK\n        if wrd:\n            self.regs[wrd] = wval\n        self.regs[0] = 0\n        self.pc = npc\n        out = {\n            'order': self.retired, 'pc': pc, 'npc': npc, 'insn': instr,\n            'rd': wrd, 'rd_wdata': wval if wrd else 0,\n            'rs1': rs1, 'rs1_rdata': rs1_rdata_pre,\n            'rs2': rs2, 'rs2_rdata': rs2_rdata_pre,\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
