{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261002-003-r9s2\ntitle: \\\"Balance the branch-condition tree feeding predictor recovery and training\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The existing agree predictor and early JAL already remove most direct\n  control-flow bubbles. A reference CoreMark profile counted 529588\n  conditional branches and only 13735 returns in the measured interval;\n  a return stack therefore offers little throughput headroom. The prior\n  r8s2 timing investigation identified the branch comparison feeding\n  predictor training and trap-qualified forwarding as a long path, but\n  changing forwarding eligibility regressed. The opportunity is to shorten\n  the predictor's outcome-resolution network while retaining its policy,\n  recovery timing and all trap-adjusted producer semantics.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the EX branch-condition comparator with a balanced\n  lexicographic tree over eight four-bit slices of the existing fully\n  forwarded, registered operands. Keep the sixteen-entry two-bit agree\n  table, its PC[5:2] indexing and reset state, early JAL, unpredicted JALR,\n  fixed-head four-entry fetch queue, and every pipeline boundary intact.\n  This is one predictor-resolution timing change; arithmetic ALU compares,\n  multiplication, division, forwarding eligibility and target generation\n  are outside its scope.\n\n  For each nibble i compute E_i=(rs1_i==rs2_i) and L_i=(rs1_i<rs2_i), with\n  unsigned four-bit operands. Combine adjacent high and low groups using\n  E=E_high & E_low and L=L_high | (E_high & L_low). Use three balanced\n  levels to produce the full-word equality and unsigned-less results.\n  Higher significance must always take priority. Derive signed-less as\n  (rs1[31] \"'!= rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_less. Select equality, its\n  complement, signed-less, its complement, unsigned-less or its complement\n  for the six legal branch funct3 values; retain false for reserved values.\n  Keep this network separate from the ALU SLT/SLTU implementation.\n\n  Feed the existing branch_cond signal with this result. Preserve all\n  downstream equations, especially branch_taken, target-alignment faults,\n  ctrl_with_trap.reg_write, fwd_w_en, effective_taken, redirect_target,\n  train_valid/train_index/train_agree and EX/MEM.pc_next. Do not repeat the\n  r8s2 producer-predicate rewrite or the r7s2 added endpoint registers.\n  A correctly predicted branch still advances without a flush. A held\n  branch neither recovers nor trains until EX advances. Recovery retains\n  priority over unavailable imem and clears the whole younger fetch queue;\n  raw payload, operand capture and source addresses remain independent of\n  redirect. Existing misalignment traps and sequential trap fallback,\n  JAL/JALR links, FENCE.I serialization and RVFI order remain authoritative.\n\n  The mechanism is parallel narrow comparisons followed by a logarithmic\n  equality/less tree, replacing a potential word-wide carry-dependent\n  branch decision. It aims to reduce late predictor-resolution delay and\n  fanout pressure without changing the cycle schedule or prediction\n  accuracy. Predict five percent higher fitness with low confidence.\n  Gowin may flatten the tree, routing can dominate, and divider launch,\n  multiply forwarding or queue controls may become limiting. The target\n  is an architectural logic change, not a circuit-neutral placement edit.\n\n  Exploratory first-placement checks rejected registered predictor\n  training, distributed binary-counter updates, prediction/strength\n  recoding, XOR indexing, static direction and one-bit agree policies:\n  they produced approximately 61-69 MHz, below the champion'\"'s 73.244 MHz\n  first placement. An earlier four-byte comparator probe reached 72.526\n  MHz and moved its worst reported path into queue control, so it did not\n  establish a fitness gain either. The proposed eight-nibble balanced\n  tree is a different comparator topology. These negative results support\n  low confidence; do not claim a measured improvement from them.\n\n  Require equivalence of the comparator across all operand bits and legal\n  branch functions, including opposite signs and equality, then run the\n  unchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates, existing unit tests, and\n  canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker/bounded-access checks with both bus\n  stall streams. Since policy and cadence are unchanged, expect exactly\n  3978988 marker-delimited CoreMark cycles. Compare all three vendor\n  placement options; acceptance above 191.27 * 1.046 = 200.06842\n  iterations/second requires median Fmax above approximately 79.607 MHz\n  at that cycle count. Preserve nret=1, all external ports, decoder\n  legality, ALTOPS/real M semantics and every existing hard invariant.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement eight parallel four-bit unsigned equality/less comparisons\n      and a three-level high-group-priority combine tree. Derive signed\n      less from sign disagreement and select the six branch conditions.\n      Drive only branch_cond with the new network. Preserve predictor\n      policy, recovery/training gating, targets, alignment faults,\n      forwarding predicates, result paths and pipeline registers exactly.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add focused branch-resolution checks for every legal comparison,\n      equality, opposite signs, signed extrema, and the highest differing\n      nibble at each of eight positions with adversarial lower nibbles.\n      Check taken/not-taken and aligned/misaligned targets, saved prediction\n      recovery, aliasing counters, once-only training through dmem holds,\n      load-dependent operands, divide completion and imem backpressure.\n      Retain all existing predictor, queue, forwarding, trap, link, RVFI\n      order, progress and wrong-path-store assertions; add a comparator\n      equivalence check without weakening any architectural checks.\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml';d=yaml.safe_load(open(p));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Validated:',p)\nprint('Required Fmax MHz:',191.27*1.046*3978988/1e7)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
